l you support the eventual nominee for the Republican Party?\par \par \uc2 HALEY: Well, I think you should ask him if he would support the eventual nominee if it was me. I mean, nobody's asked him that, and I think that's the case.\par \par \uc2 Look, the conventions not till July. There's a lot of time. I mean, I have said very clearly how much I think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a problem, how I think he's dangerous for our country, and how I think we need to go in a different direction. But I don't think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should be president, that's why I'm running. And I don't think a lot of other people think the same thing.\par \par \uc2 Millions of people will vote tomorrow, and they're going to have their voices heard. This is not anti-Trump movement. This is a pro American movement. These are people who are tired of the wasteful spending. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's not talking about the fact that he put us $8 trillion in debt in four years. These are people who want to go and see a secure border, and they don't like the fact that Trump stopped Congress from trying to fix the bill and pass a strong border bill.\par \par \uc2 This is about national security, where we should be preventing war, and Trump said he would stand with Putin as he invaded our allies. It's a totally different set of policies that we're talking about that we want to see America go in a strong direction. And so, I think people have the chance to vote tomorrow, and it's going to be a great day.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: You know, I know that you've ruled out running in any kind of third party and giving people another alternative, but here are some folks who really would like one. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW, NORTH CAROLINA VOTER: I'd vote third party.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Third party?\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Right in or third party?\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW: Well, if Nikki doesn't