 copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020240301ek2t00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden's Incompetency Coverup; Biden Promises, But Never Delivers; Dem CA Rep Barbara Lee Wants $50 Minimum Wage; Democrats Hope Lawfare Can Derail Trump's 2024 Momentum; Juge Weighs Tossing \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  Off Trump Georgia Case; Willis' Affair Jeopardizes Her Role In Trump Case; Ex-Hunter Business Partners Testify Against Joe; Bobulinski Attorney Accuses Democrats Of Lying; What Does China Have On The Bidens; Actor Mark Wahlberg Joins The Angle; Hallow Prayer App Surges After Super Bowl Ad\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham, Bill Melugin, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 7,949 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 6 PM in the East, 3 PM on the West Coast. My thanks to Kevin Corke for the top of the show. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced, and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle is now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle. Thank you for joining us tonight. Old dog, old tricks. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 On inauguration day, the Biden team promised that with Trump gone, things in government would go back to normal. That meant leveling all the time with the American people.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: His objective, and his commitment is to bring transparency and truth back to government to share the truth even when it's hard to hear. And that's something that I hope to deliver on in this role as well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It all sounded so wonderful. But three years later, we see those were just words signifying nothing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Folks, you're going to ask me questions, hang on a second. I'm going to be back on Thursday, I'm not going to be answering any questions in this. I'll be back Thursday to stand here with you and answer all the questions you want about this issue.\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon. Before I begin, I'm going to make this statement, let it stand on its own. I'm not going to take any questions, but I'll be taking questions tomorrow or the next day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Biden reminds me of that cartoon character, you know, from decades and decades and decades ago, the one who was always putting off paying up.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I gladly pay you Tuesday for a hamburger today.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, it's a classic Biden bait and switch. I'll actually answer questions later, if you promised to just sit and listen today. But of course, later never comes.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I promise, I'll come back and answer questions later. Thank you,\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Sir. When Trump said that sir --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What's plan B if the speaker doesn't act?\par \par \uc2 CROWD: (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And every now and then the White House is actually stunned that a reporter actually calls Biden on his wimpy style promise.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The President said yesterday that he would be taking questions today or tomorrow. What was he referring to?\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: I don't have anything to share at this time, as you know, the President takes questions from you all, often. I don't have anything on the public schedule to speak to.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Sorry, I don't have anything on the public schedule to speak to. Now, if she as press secretary doesn't know what's on the President's public schedule. Who does? Who we supposed to call?\par \par \uc2 Now no one on earth really believes that she doesn't know why Biden avoids unscripted Q&As with reporters, because we all know when Joe speaks, he wanders. And when Joe walks, he wanders, and his mind wanders as well.\par \par \uc2 Now remember, when he lashed out at Special Prosecutor Hur for asking about the date of his son's death which he couldn't recall?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: He even referenced that I don't remember when my son died. How in the hell dare he raised that? Frankly, when I was asked the question, I thought to myself, was there any other damn business?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, the enablers, of course, rushed in to echo Biden's indignation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I find the shots on his memory, particularly a shot about when did \uc2 Beau Biden\uc2  die beneath any special counsel?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Why the hell you're asking that question?\par \par \uc2 AL SHARPTON\uc2 , CIVIL RIGHTS ACTIVIST: Why would he even be questioning \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  about when did his son die?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It turns out, the prosecutor did not ask that question. Sources are telling NBC News that it was Biden himself who raised his son's death when trying to recall when he discovered classified docs at the rental home. Well, Biden brought up the timing of Beau's death, then he couldn't recall the year.\par \par \uc2 The First Lady even sent out a fundraising appeal decrying the use of their son's death to score political points. Now, this is all absurd. Either Biden forgot the details of his interview with the special prosecutor, or he's being purposely deceptive and trying to make money off of a craven false storyline. Whatever the truth, the old dog can't learn new tricks and won't answer for anything.\par \par \uc2 There's an audio tape of the special prosecutor interview, we understand. Release it, Mr. President, as Trump released his Ukraine call when questions arose about that. But Biden doesn't answer real questions, because he literally can't. He makes none of the major decisions, not about Ukraine, not about China, not about the border, not about the economy. The entire White House is run by some, I don't know, some amalgam of Jill Biden, a few key staffers, and of course the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Of course, one way to alleviate the concerns about Biden's mental condition would be for him to just submit to a basic cognitive test. But the White House, they already nixed that. To shift the narrative away from Biden's feeble condition, they're hoping that other octogenarians can really help rally the base.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2  (D-CA): We have a great candidate, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , President of the United States; \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , we're on the road to victory, as I say, but we just win baby. We have a will to win, and we will win, because it is the right thing for our country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is it just me or does Anderson Cooper there look like he's just going to burst out laughing. But it is true, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is the paragon of mental clarity, so she does know best.\par \par \uc2 But the award for the lamest \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  rescue effort goes to Politico. In a piece today, they try to equate Trump's occasional verbal missteps that we all make to Biden's persistent and glaring mental lapses, which, look, this is just ludicrous on its face, I'm not going to spend time on that. And then they -- by the way, they prattle on about how awesome Biden is behind closed-doors. How many times have we heard this? They, quote, Mayor Pete saying that Biden stumped an expert from the \uc2 Federal Railroad Administration\uc2  behind closed-doors, who couldn't answer all of Biden's questions. So, that expert had to dial in another expert just to answer Joe's tough questions.\par \par \uc2 Now, are we to believe that Mayor Pete, who wouldn't know a locomotive from a caboose is now suddenly a geriatric care specialist. Now, let's be clear, the claim that Biden is sharper than he appears is simply a lie. It's an insult to everyone's intelligence. But look at the voters want to be treated with more respect; they are going to have to pick a different president. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now and I'm delighted he's with us, Texas Congressman and former White House physician, \uc2 Ronny Jackson\uc2 . Congressman, I know you've spoken out about this. But a cognitive test that the White House has essentially dismissed out of hand, what would that tell us about his current state of mind, his condition?\par \par \uc2 REP. RONNY JACKSON (R-TX): Well, I think Laura, it would tell us exactly what we all already know. And I'm not even sure that we need the cognitive test anymore. Everyone in the country knows what's going on right now. It would tell us that he's not fit to be our president, our commander-in-chief and our head of state. It's unfortunate, you know, but I maintain that President Trump had to do a cognitive test that the press just went crazy demanding, and I was a physician at the time demanding that he have a cognitive test on his part of his physical exam, because they didn't like his personality. They didn't like his style, not because he did anything that was concerning on a cognitive level.\par \par \uc2 But they've set the precedent now. And I think that I told him today at a press conference today, and I said, I want to see the same enthusiasm and the same insistence that President Biden get a cognitive test on now. Because if we've ever had a sitting president that needs a cognitive test, it's right now, and this is an absolute disaster. And I've been saying this, and you've heard me say it 1000 times, I've been saying this since he was candidate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . This man's not fit to be our president.\par \par \uc2 He's continued to demonstrate to the entire world over and over, over the last three and a half years if that's the case. Now we have the Hur report, completely different angle, an appointee from his own DOJ that's basically saying the same thing now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to --\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, I want to point out that the White House said in response today, Congressman, you just got out a mouthful there. In a statement of Fox Digital, they compared you to a Simpsons' character, basically saying you have no credibility, implying that you kind of fudged Trump's cognitive test, and that you have no credibility on this. Your response.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: It's absolutely ridiculous. And, you know, Laura, I was at the White House. I was a White House physician for 14 years. I took care of President Bush for three years. I took care of President \uc2 Obama\uc2  for eight years, and I took care of President Bush for three -- President Trump for three years. So, I was there 14 years for three different administrations, including eight years in the \uc2 Obama\uc2  administration in which I was the appointed physician to the President for \uc2 Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most of these people, a lot of these people in the West Wing right now with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I took care of them, they were they -- so for them to make that claim is ridiculous, it doesn't surprise me that they spend all their time watching the same --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, they're smearing you.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, they're smearing you.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to point out something that Chris Matthews on MSNBC said this morning, he had advice for Biden staffers and on the other side, I'm going to ask you whether that would work. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS MATTHEWS, MSNBC ANCHOR: Biden is going to get out there and mix it up. He's going to have to get on the corner and meet people and hanging out with regular people. He's going to do it. Now, he may make some problems along the way. He will make more gaffes. Of course, he will. But is it better to have him out there? You know, if I'm in a back room with him, I'd make him feel better about himself. I just be just nice to him and encouraging that's one thing, but staffers should do, encourage the guy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now Congressman, if someone is declining because of various aging issues, I mean, everyone wants to be encouraged. But does that get at the fundamental problem here that we know he's not making the big decisions here?\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Well, yes, it begs the question of who's making these decisions? I think the whole world and I mean, the world, not just this country, realizes this particular point that he's not calling the shots. He's not making the decisions. And so, I think that -- the world is in chaos right now, we've got a lot of stuff going on. We need somebody who's attuned to what's happening, who's read into everything that's going on. And he can make these decisions and multi-task, and this guy obviously cannot do this. So, it's very concerning. It's a national security issue for us right now. We're going to get in trouble.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well --\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Here in the near future. We've got all kinds of stuff going on.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want to -- I want everyone to also think about this for a moment that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  offered to do the Super Bowl interview.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He said, I'll do it. Biden won't do it. I'll do it. Of course, \uc2 CBS\uc2  immediately just rejected that idea, because everybody knows that Trump can go toe-to-toe with some of them. He was on with Kaitlan Collins and did that that town hall, all -- it's like the media doesn't want him to speak out because they're afraid he's going to convince people, but they want Biden and they're perfectly fine with Biden not doing these big events, because they know it's going to make him look even worse. But with Trump, it's the opposite. They don't really want him out there. And I'm going to ask him some tough questions at our town hall.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: No, I mean, the contrast is crazy. Trump can walk up to a gaggle of reporters completely not knowing --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: -- what they're going to ask him, answer questions for hours, hours on end, and Biden --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Totally.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: -- can't stand in front of a teleprompter and read the teleprompter without looking horrible, just in a matter of minutes. They just try to whisk him out, whisk him back. So, I mean, it's crazy. The contrast between these two people, between President Trump and Biden could not be more obvious in the entire American people -- everyone in this country, everyone in the world sees this contrast, and so, they can try to make the argument --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's --\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: -- all day long, that you know, but it's just not sticking. People know what they see.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, thank you. Great to see you. All right, the big parades of the Kansas City Chiefs Super Bowl win turned into chaos today after a shooting left at least one dead and 22 injured. Fox News National Correspondent Bill Melugin is standing by with all the details, Bill?\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Well, Laura, the shooting happened right at the end of the \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  celebration. The gunfire could actually be heard on live TV and livestreams, and it sent people running in all sorts of different directions.\par \par \uc2 According to Kansas City Fire officials, there are at least 22 victims who were injured in the shooting, eight with immediate life-threatening injuries, seven with life-threatening injuries, and at least one person has died. Local media reporting many of the injured are children.\par \par \uc2 Authorities say as it stands right now at least three people are in custody in connection with the shooting. They've also recovered at least one firearm. The motive and what initially caused this is all still under investigation.\par \par \uc2 Now, video posted to social media appears to show bystanders tracking and tackling one of the possible suspected shooters as he was running through a crowd. Two men can be seen taking him to the ground and pinning him to the ground until police arrive a second social media video shows police surrounding that same suspect and taking him into custody. Bystanders can be heard in the background saying they tackled him and that a gun was recovered. Witnesses described what they saw when those shots rang out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This family came up to us, mom, dad and like a nine- year-old and like a five-year-old, and they were bawling. And they said we just saw somebody get shot in the lawn. When I saw those kids faces about somebody getting hurt, like they were tarnished, and they were like scared.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: And Kansas City Police say the White House has been in touch with them and is offering all necessary federal resources. Meantime, the \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  did release a statement confirming that all of their players, staff, and coaches are safe. We'll send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Bill, unbelievably shocking. Thank you. All right, new details about who Biden is replacing U.S. born citizens within our workforce. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  reacts, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: So far, we've created 14 million new jobs, more jobs in three years than any presidents created in four years in history. We're investing in America, and jobs for American workers built with American products.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Biden sounding almost Trumpian there, all that focus on American workers. Gee, it almost sounds too good to be true. Because it is. New analysis is showing, get this, nearly 3 million migrants have joined the workforce since January 2020. And what about the native born American employment? Well, it actually dropped by 121,000 during that same timeframe.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , former Senior Advisor to President Trump, founder of America First Legal, Stephen, and to add insult to injury, Colorado is now floating a plan to hire non-citizens to serve as police officers and firefighters. Stephen, it's America last once again for these people.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FOUNDER, AMERICA FIRST LEGAL: Absolutely, Laura, and let's talk about something that very few people actually know about. In 2020, President Trump issued a travel ban on foreign workers, a 212(f) travel ban on foreign workers, so guests, workers, green card based employment workers, et cetera, saying that they couldn't come into the country and take jobs during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 He did this specifically knowing that companies would try to replace American workers with lower costs foreign workers using their pandemic as a pretext. When \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  came into office, what did he do? Not only did he open up the southern border completely, as we know, adding in 10 plus million illegals, but he also canceled all of President Trump's economic travel bans to let in massive numbers of foreign workers, including foreign guest workers to pay who earn wages far beneath what Americans earn.\par \par \uc2 The result, as you have said, is that all of the jobs recovery since the pandemic, all of it, 100 percent, Laura, has gone to migrant laborers. There are fewer U.S. born Americans working today than there were --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's just --\par \par \uc2 MILLER: -- before the pandemic. So, every time Biden talks about the economy, all of that, all of that is the employment of migrant workers.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And they're -- the sanctuary mayors in these cities have been pushing for expedited work permits for migrants. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ERIC ADAMS (D), MAYOR, NEW YORK CITY: We're saying we must expedite rote (ph) visas. It's just common sense. Thousands of jobs are available to be filled.\par \par \uc2 MIKE JOHNSTON (D), MAYOR, DENVER: What we want is the federal government to step out of the way of employers who want to hire individuals who are trying to get access to work and help get them access to work as expediently as possible.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, he echoed that again today, especially given that story about the police officers and firefighters jobs going to non-citizens. Let's get a move into the workplace. That means Stephen, they'll never leave, they're going to say they can't be deported, et cetera, et cetera. So, in meshing them in American culture, this was the plan all along.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: First of all, we've entered a brave new world now, where the not too distant future illegal aliens will be arresting American citizens. That is the world that we are entering right now. And 