o on a date, and we'll spend a little time together. But I only had a lunch break. I wanted to take her to church. I took her to St. Patrick's, but she thought that this is a new approach to, you know, trying to -- trying to make a good impression.\par \par \uc2 But honestly, I was going to church and I wanted to, and that -- you know, I prayed for to meet somebody that I could actually, you know, really start a family, and without the -- the fame and the popularity, like, to get to know me.\par \par \uc2 And then we got married in the church. I proposed in the church. And so, yeah.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And you're off to the races. The family is thriving. J-Lo just released that three-part documentary and musical piece celebrating her love for Ben Affleck.\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: Oh nice.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You're going to bring the funky bunch back together and do that for Rhea?\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: You know, I think my wife would stop talking to me if I did that.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I would stop talking to you.\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: But that being said, you know, I always try to do everything I can to not only embarrass her a little bit but make her laugh. I just started doing a couple little silly dances the other day and she was like, hysterical laughing on the floor.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, that's part of keeping the romance alive.\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Thank you for being with us.\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: Thank you, sir. I appreciate it very much.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Have a happy Lent. And thanks for keeping us all prayed on.\par \par \uc2 WAHLBERG: Thank you. That's nice to see, rolled right off the tongue there.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Right. Well, I hear you say it all the time, of course. I got my line down.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You know, Laura, a lot of people love the fact that you have somebody of Wahlberg stature speaking out about his faith, the source of his success, and keep