 receives due process.\par \par \uc2 So, it's not about whether it was the right verdict, which it was, it's how we got there. And if we're OK with jurors being tampered with and impacting their decision, like we heard in the clip, then you better be OK with it when it affects your family. When someone you love challenges the state or the government and the process is unfair. But you got to be OK with it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Mark, even one juror, and I share your thoughts on this, I mean, you have to have a unanimous verdict. So, if one juror says, we were rushed, I felt pressured, I mean, it's pretty bad. I mean, at the very least, it's really bad.\par \par \uc2 EIGLARSH: I can live with rushed. I can live with even pressured because jurors feel that. What I can't live with is Hill, a clerk who spewed unlawfully words that impacted these jurors. How dare she do that. And worse to have the courage, this jury had the courage to come forward and say, you know what, it really did influence my decision.\par \par \uc2 If that's a fact, then that is a denial of due process. It is a denial of what we stand for in this country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Mark, jurors claim they also were allowed to have their cell phones during the trial. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I understand that during the testimony of the first juror, some opened their cell phones in the jury room, in our jury assembly room here. Were you one who opened her cell phone?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Yes, ma'am.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Did you listen to the -- or watch the broadcast of that first juror's examination?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I was on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Ma'am?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I was on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I was on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , I guess. Your thoughts?\par \par \uc2 EIGLARSH: Ay, ay. Further evidence that if you like justice, like hot dogs, don't go see how it's made. It's really gross. You know, this whole process. And again, I don't want Alex Murdaugh to have a new trial. I don't. The expense? I, you know, just -- in terms of money and emotion, but how do you not?\par \par \uc2 If this is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and we know we have a lot of people who want him to get fair trials, if this is your child who goes through this, are you OK with the tampering of jurors? There's no way, if you're being intellectually honest, that you are.\par \par \uc2 So, you got to stand up and speak for this situation because it applies to every other person in the criminal justice arena.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, that Becky Hill is a piece of work there, Mark. Unbelievable. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 EIGLARSH: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Coming up, could the Super Bowl or a particular fan impact the next election? And Biden finds religion even as he gets lost. Seen and Unseen with Raymond, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for Seen and Unseen, where we reveal the stories behind the headlines. And for that, we turn to Fox News contributor Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond, Biden, he's hitting the campaign trail hard.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yeah, I'm afraid it's hitting back just as hard, Laura. President Biden was campaigning in South Carolina ahead of the weekend's primary, but it may have been wiser to just send a statement instead.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: There are still too many corporations in America ripping people off. You see that article about the Snickers bar? Well, it's going to stop. America, we're tired of being played for suckers. Let me tell you who else is noticing that. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Did you see what he recently said about that he wants to see the economy crash this year? A sitting president.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He's a sitting president, Laura. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. I don't even know what -- did I miss a story about Snickers? And I love Snickers, especially when they're in the freezer. Take them off the freezer. Those are good.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: There was a piece in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  about inflation and Snickers, and of course, he just reduced all of that to Snickers. It's going to stop. OK. On Sunday, Biden tried to reach out to black voters by claiming that he went to mass, Laura, and then attended a black Baptist Church. Things didn't improve much on Sunday when he spoke to the church in Columbia in South Carolina, and he told these old stories. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: You all think I'm kidding. The longest time, when I was a young public defender and a United States Senator, I went to, excuse me, AME church, I apologize. But all kidding aside, then I'd go to 10:30 Mass, 10:30 service with Reverend Beeman. And, you know -- you said it, Rev, my mother would say, you got to be who you say you are.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. Well, that's the problem, Laura. Is he being who he says he is? Three years ago, he claimed he went to 8 o'clock mass and then attended a church, a Union Baptist Church in Wilmington, only no one there remembers him ever attending that church. So, this is a very tough moment for the president, trying to be who he's not.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He needs divine intervention just to get through these speeches at this point.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, not only through them, Laura, if he's so familiar with the black church, he might have had an easier time figuring out how to exit the pulpit. He really had a difficult time here. He doesn't know whether to go left or right or genuflect. Look, where do I go? OK, yeah.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It looks like -- what's that \uc2 Disney\uc2 , the Disney Hall of Presidents? Is that what it is? He almost moves like those.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He does. He has that very stiff -- well, and exits are a problem, you're right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Ray, last week Biden visited with those union workers. And social media, they lit up with all these reports that Biden put the hard hat on backwards.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. Well, the website, Snopes, quickly rushed in claiming this was false. The internal suspension, they said, on the helmet was just sticking out. Well, now they're walking that back. They've done an about face on the hard hat. And we can now verify, Laura, this is how you wear the hat. Not like this. Which we had that tight. He's literally got it on backwards.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's -- where is that? I don't even see him. Oh, there he is. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: In the middle.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's got -- I mean, well, what do you got to do?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It looks like a cardboard cutout there? But isn't that pathetic that you have to -- that you have to actually go to Snopes to get them to correct their correction. I mean, it's just sad.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's the major reaction of the indefensible. It makes no --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: My goodness. Well, speaking of helmets, do you watch any of the big games over the weekend? I did.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah. You mean tracking Taylor Swift's movements? I missed it. But \uc2 CBS\uc2  certainly milked every moment. The displeasure of Ms. Swift is so abundant and obvious. Watch her lips as the broadcast continues.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: With the -- she's going to be there at the Grammys. She could break the record for the most -- album of the year wins. Find out, live, next Sunday right here on \uc2 CBS\uc2 . It's streaming --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Go away, please.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, she was happy at the end though. They had a big smooch. That was a nice moment.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, you know, Laura --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I like her. I know she's kind of liberal, I guess. She shouldn't be liberal. She should be a total conservative, given what -- given everything.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, look, people can quibble about whether she's good for the game, she's bad for the game. That all can be debated. But there's no debate that the Biden administration is now saying privately and publicly they would like to use Taylor Swift and get her endorsement. This has been in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Newsweek. Everybody's reporting on this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course. Well, I should hope that -- yeah. You'd be dumb not to want it.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Because there's a poll. There's that poll where 18 percent of the electorate says they would follow her endorsement, and three out of ten people under 35. If they can get the Taylor Swift endorsement, they think they can push them over the finish line, but I'd talk to Marcia Blackburn first, whom she defied and flamed out spectacularly.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Well, she has a good brand management style. The Bidens could learn from Taylor Swift. See you tomorrow night. Jesse is next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020240130ek1t00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 New White House Reaction As Border Showdown Intensifies; Harris Accuses GOP Of Politicizing Border Crisis; Governor Noem: Southern Border Is A "War Zone"; Governor Noem: Proud Of Texas For Defending Itself; Awaiting Verdict On Trump Defamation Damages; Netanyahu: Israel Has A Right To Defend Itself; White House On UNRWA Staff Allegations; US Pauses Aid To \uc2 UN\uc2  After Claims Vs Staff; Hunger Strike For Political Prisoners In Iran; Rep. Phillips On Why He's Challenging Biden; Fake Taylor Swift Sex Photos Go Viral\b0\par\par\uc2 Trace Gallagher, Peter Doocy, Matt Finn, Matt Whitaker, Tom Homan,  Alexis McAdams, Alex Hogan, Jonathan Hunt \par \uc2 7,847 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 January 2024\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: The Story with Martha MacCallum\par \uc2 HUNDD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: And I can't even believe that does it for us. Two hours flew by, Gillian, great to have you here today and --\par \par \uc2 GILLIAN TURNER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Yes, no, it's been great and we hope you have a great weekend, set your DVR and never miss AMERICA REPORTS, and thanks so much for joining us. I'm Sandra Smith.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: I'm Gillian Turner, THE STORY starts right now. Trace Gallagher in for Martha.\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Gillian and Sandra, thank you. Good afternoon, everybody. I'm Trace Gallagher in for Martha MacCallum, and this is THE STORY.\par \par \uc2 New reaction from the White House to the standoff underway right now at our southern border. Today is the deadline for Texas Governor Greg Abbott to allow federal agents access to Shelby Park. That's in Eagle Pass, a hub for illegal border crossings. The Biden administration wants the razor wire fencing there gone, but defiant Texas officials now declaring they will not comply.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the National Guard there is putting up more razor wire. Matt Finn is live on the ground with more on that. Our panel is standing by \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2 , Tom Homan and Tomi Lahren. But first, to the White House correspondent, Peter Doocy, who is directly out of the White House briefing. Peter, good afternoon.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Good afternoon, Trace. We know that half of this country's governors, 25 of them, all Republicans, sent a letter to this president saying that they stand with Governor Abbott in this effort to secure the border on his own. But it doesn't sound like this White House is putting any stock at all in that letter. Instead, they keep directing people's attentions to these Senate negotiations on the border that, based on everything that we're hearing, are dead.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: If they truly want to help with the issue at the border, with the immigration system, that they need to talk to their, they need to talk to the congressional members, the senators in their state. That's what they need to do. They need to ask them to make sure that they have the resources they need within their respective states to take action, right, to actually deal with a broken system. The way that we deal with this is legislatively.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voiceover): Part of this letter from the 25 governors say this: "We stand in solidarity with our fellow governor Greg Abbott and the state of Texas in utilizing every tool and strategy, including razor wire fences to secure the border. We do it in part because the Biden administration is refusing to enforce immigration laws already on the books and is illegally allowing mass parole across America of migrants who entered our country illegally." One of the governors who signed that letter in Oklahoma speaking out about it.\par \par \uc2 GOV. KEVIN STITT (R-OK): In Texas, there's 28 ports of entry and it's already a federal law that it's illegal to enter anywhere but those points of entry. I mean, the last time I flew to Mexico, I had to land at an airport and show them my passport and so the fact that the federal government, Biden, is cutting razor wire it just makes no sense at all. And so, yes, we have the right to defend our country against invasion. And what else would you call it if you've got six million people coming through illegally?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: President Biden has said nothing about this today. In fact, he said nothing about it all week. Trace.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Peter Doocy live for us in the White House. Peter, thank you. Let's go live to the ground now to Eagle Pass, Texas, and the national correspondent, Matt Finn. Matt, good afternoon.\par \par \uc2 MATT FINN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Good afternoon, Trace. Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  is here on site in Shelby Park. We just saw her doing a tour on an airboat not long ago. She is one of those Republican governors who has publicly declared that she stands with Texas Governor Greg Abbott. And as of this hour, Texas has not relinquished control of this park. The Texas National Guard is still fiercely defending this park both on the street and along the Rio Grande River. It has not removed any razor wire. In fact, it is installing additional razor wire right now.\par \par \uc2 Today is the deadline that the Biden administration issued to the state of Texas to respond to the federal government regarding how much, or if any, of this park it plans on reopening to the federal government. And the Texas Attorney General tells me as it stands right now, they have no plans in place to reopen this park to the federal government. One point of contention is the boat launch here. Texas says that the \uc2 United States government\uc2  has had access to the boat launch and it has access to the river.\par \par \uc2 The state of Texas just does not want the Biden administration interfering with its mission on land or interfering with its razor wire. Also, worth noting this afternoon that a U.S. Customs and Border Patrol source tells Fox News that Border Patrol does not plan on coming here into this park and removing razor wire. Rather, it just wants to remove it or cut it during emergency situations. It's worth noting that that's what got us here in the first place. Texas does not want the Biden administration touching the razor wire at all. Trace.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, so, the -- so, we're clear Matt, nobody right now is trying to get in the park and do anything with the razor wire. So, Texas is holding their ground, but nobody is actively trying to get in that park.\par \par \uc2 FINN: Right, correct. The Texas National Guard is fiercely protecting this park. We have to show identification just to get in here. There's no one knocking on the fence trying to get in here to tear down the razor wire, but Texas is making it clear that it does not want Border Patrol touching the razor wire at all moving forward, Trace.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Got it. Matt Finn live for us in Eagle Pass. Matt, thank you. Let's bring in our panel. \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2 , former acting attorney general under President Trump. Tom Homan, former acting ICE Director, and Tomi Lahren, host of "Tomi Lahren is Fearless" on OutKick, both are Fox News Contributors. Here is Texas Governor Greg Abbott talking about states' rights. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. GREG ABBOTT (R-TX): The authors of the Constitution knew there would be times when the federal government would not live up to its duty, and so they empowered states in Article 1, Section 10, the right of self-defense. And what Texas is asserting is our Article 1, Section 10 right of self- defense, because the President of the United States is not fulfilling his duty to enforce the laws passed by Congress that deny illegal entry into the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, and he's getting backing now \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2  from 25 governors, is it a fair argument?\par \par \uc2 MATT WHITAKER\uc2 , FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, I think it's actually a legitimate argument. Obviously, we want law and order on the southern border, and we had it in the trump administration we work very hard to plus up ICE lawyers and the judges that serve in the immigration courts at DOJ. But ultimately, we've had, this is a complete crisis that was created by the Biden administration. And 100,000 known gotaways is too many, and think about the unknown gotaways that are incomprehensible, and this is just, that has to stop.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, and we should also point out that we still have not gotten December's numbers. Maybe they'll drop today, maybe they'll let them out. Tom Homan, to you, at the very heart of this issue is national security. We don't know who these people are or what their intent is, and yet they are coming by the millions.\par \par \uc2 TOM HOMAN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: And this is why it's a national security issue. You know, since Biden's been in the White House, we're just shy of two million, two million gotaways. And here's what you need to consider. Border Patrol's arrested people from 181 different countries. Some of these countries are sponsors of a terror. And Border Patrol's arrested over 300 on the southern border alone since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's been in the White House.\par \par \uc2 Under Trump, we got 11 in four years, 11. So, with 300 arrested and two million gotaways, how many of those gotaways came from a country sponsored terror? If you think it's zero, then you're not paying attention to the data. This is the biggest national security failure I've seen since 9-11. So, march on, Governor Abbott, you're doing the right thing for the state of Texas and the United States.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes, I mean, listen, we don't know the exact number, but you're right, it's not zero. And because we don't know the exact number, it becomes even more frightening for us. Tomi Lahren, to you, because now the administration, the Biden administration, after three years of keeping the border wide open, is now saying the GOP wants to keep the border open because they want to run on it. Here's \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We have right now a proposal for $14 billion. We hope and are really trying to compel, in particular, some of the Republicans in Congress, to participate in the solution. But sadly, you know, we want to fix it. They want to run on it. They want a political issue to run on in November.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Those who cover the border, like we have for many, many years, realize that there's no bill you can pass that is going to stop the flow of migrants. You have to secure the border, Tomi.\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, HOST, OUTKICK: Right, and this is not a money issue. You hear Democrats talking about how they want to throw more money at the problem, more Border Patrol agents at the problem, but it's not Border Patrol agents, as Tom very well knows, that are going to do their job. It's Border Patrol agents that are going to have their hands tied behind their back or act as an escort service for the illegals coming in.\par \par \uc2 This is not a money issue. We don't need more money to process illegals faster for catch and release. We need to secure our border and God bless Texas for doing the hard work here. Exit poll after exit poll shows us that immigration is the top issue, even in some cases ahead of the economy for voters coming up. So, this is going to be an election issue, but God bless Texas and God bless these governors that are standing beside Governor Greg Abbott and finally doing what this administration has failed to do.\par \par \uc2 And when these Democrats talk about how Republicans are standing in the way, there is not a Republican out there that believes the Biden administration, no matter what they pass, is going to enforce anything because they could be enforcing it now. They're not enforcing the laws already on the books. Secure the border. God bless Texas. Do what you have to do. And thank you for protecting this nation.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: I got about 60 seconds left. Like to get all three of you in on this because Trump is right when he says that at least the remain in Mexico and building the wall, at least directed these migrants in the right direction where they can get some help. For you, you first, \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WHITAKER: Yes, well that's absolutely true. And remember, if the Biden administration was doing all it could and we still had a crisis, I think then we could look to Congress for more tools. But they have all the tools they need.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes. Tom Homan.\par \par \uc2 HOMAN: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said the Republicans need to help with the solution, they have the solution, it's called HR-2. The House passed it. And, and we know it's going to work because most of HR-2 is the Trump policies that we prove were the most effective things on the border. So, HR-2 is there Kamala, have the Senate pass that. President sign it, secure the border.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: But they took everything down as soon as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got into office. Tomi Lahren, your final thoughts on this?\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: Yes, Remain in Mexico not only works for us, but it also incentivizes Mexico to do their part. They will do their part if they have some pressure. So, maybe threaten some tariffs, have Remain in Mexico, get them to play ball, and we can start in the path of securing this nation.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Tomi Lahren, Tom Homan, \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2 , thank you all. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, South Dakota Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  said here that she would travel more than 1,000 miles to deliver Governor Abbott razor wire and help secure the border. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. KRISTI NOEM (R-SD): This is incredibly important and Governor Abbott has done the exact right thing and I'll drive him more razor wire from South Dakota if I have to for him to do his job.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Well, guess what? The governor has just arrived in Eagle Pass and joins us live. They're micing her up right now. Next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Well, at least half of America's governors now backing Texas Governor Greg Abbott in his battle with the Biden administration over securing the border. They are all Republicans. South Dakota Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  is among them. She is at the border today in Eagle Pass, and she calls it a warzone.\par \par \uc2 Governor, great of you to join us. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 You say that you are proud of what Texas is doing. Tell us why.\par \par \uc2 GOV. KRISTI NOEM (R-SD): I am. I'm incredibly proud of Texas and the actions that they're taking. They're protecting their state's sovereignty.\par \par \uc2 Listen, this is Texas land. Shelby Park belongs to the State of Texas. It's a part of the United States of America, and the President is refusing to defend it from an invasion.\par \par \uc2 So, today was the deadline that President Biden gave Texas to -- that they're going to start cutting down some of the razor wire. There has been none of that happening here today. But, I, as the governor of South Dakota see the effects of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ignoring federal law and allowing this invasion every single day in my home state.\par \par \uc2 The funneling of the human trafficking and the drugs comes across