ers he alleged did not identify themselves as officers of the law. He calls the cops which are now seeing on video right there. And what happens, Chris, he ends up being arrested for the alleged assault in the first encounter.\par \par \uc2 KACHOUROFF: Right, because and that's the odd thing is they have a state police arrest him for a state crime. And then just shortly before -- I mean, that was 10 hours after he made the report, so you can imagine his surprise that he now gets arrested. And then knowing how embarrassing it must look to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to have the state police make the arrest shortly before the court case in Maryland, in the state level, we've got a phone call that said, they're dismissing that case and they're going to indict him federally and so he's got misdemeanor charges pending right now at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 And I've heard that they want to now upgrade it to a felony. So, it's crazy to me. I mean, like I said, no police officer worth his salt, even an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent is going to do this type of shenanigans. I call it a shenanigan. It's very suspicious that they didn't make a report themselves.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: All right, Chris. We really appreciate you being with us tonight, sharing this story in that video with our audience. Thank you. Coming up, another batch of Epstein documents have been unsealed and we'll bring you the latest developments. Plus, we're going to cut through Biden economic spin. That's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: There has been a lot of pessimism about the economy that's really proven unwarranted.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's going to take a little bit of time for folks to feel what the Bidenomics has been able to do.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAIN: More time. More time to feel the effects of Bidenomics. Americans don't need more time. They need more money in their pocket. But since Team Biden is back out in full force, bragging about his disastrous economy, we thought it might be a good time to cut through the spin, debunk Bidenomics. So first up, gas prices.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Gas prices, for example, are at 3.09 today, more than $1.93 lower than the peak after Putin's war.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Joining me now is David Asman, Fox Business host and former Wall Street Journal senior editor.\par \par \uc2 DAVID ASMAN, FOX BUSINESS ANCHOR: Isn't it wonderful that they get experts like Granholm to head up institutions that are based on stuff that they haven't got a clue about before they got into the job?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Well, clue us in. What's the truth on gas prices?\par \par \uc2 ASMAN: Well, gas prices. Let's talk oil because gas, of course, comes from oil. Crude oil was trading at $40 a barrel on the day that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was elected. $40 a barrel. The traders -- oil traders got nervous because he said he was going to have a war on fossil fuels, which he has in many parts. So, it went up 30 percent to $52 a barrel at the time of his inauguration.\par \par \uc2 Then it's now trading at about 72. Of course, it did spike to over $100 a barrel when Russia invaded Ukraine. It's true it did spike, but it's now at $72. $72 a barrel is 63 percent more than when he was elected and 38 percent more than when he became president.\par \par \uc2 So, we're not paying less right now. We're paying less than at the height after Russia invaded Ukraine, but we're not paying less than when he came in. We're paying a lot more, 63 percent when he was elected, 38 percent more when he became president.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: It's a truth that people feel at the gas pump.\par \par \uc2 ASMAN: It's just one -- one of many, many canards that they come out with.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Let's stay on the auto theme. Let's look under the hood of today's jobs report. The Biden administration want you to think it's a good one. We see that