ving it as it is. There are votes to be gained for Democrats. And you see that this alliance of the Henry Cuellars of the world and \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , and you have \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , saying I'm going to send the National Guard down to the border.\par \par \uc2 FAILLA: Listen, I knew something was up when \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2  left the nightclub. Then we were like, wow, right this is out of control.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: With a Turkish sate or no?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MONTGOMERY: That's when you knew this was serious.\par \par \uc2 All right, I'm pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  crowd are some serious party poopers blocking traffic at two major airports and scheming to ruin your New Year's Eve plans. Don't you dare commies, that's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: From the river to the sea, Palestine will be free.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HURT: Get ready to ring in the New Year with pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  agitators? The anti- Israel crew is getting a practice run on what they hope to do this New Year's Eve. Dozens of them getting arrested for blocking roadways outside major travel hubs, including New York City's JFK Airport.\par \par \uc2 They also made life pretty miserable for travelers at LAX. The blockades forcing some fliers to burst through the signs on foot to bypass jam Broadway (PH).\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, we might see this type of nonsense as we count down to 2024. Protesters are expected to target the Times Square ball drop. But Mayor Adams promises that the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  will be on top of things.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ADAMS: There's always a serious concern around safety in New Year's Eve, because there's a large number of people. Everyone, you know, look for events like this if they want to do bad things. And the police department is on top of it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HURT: Yes, we'll see. Look, t