underlying problem to it, and that there's no discipline, there's no law enforcement, and there's no mandate of the treatment that people with mental illness and drug addiction need in order to get into recovery.\par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR: Yes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM: OK. Kellyanne, let's start here. He says that -- the governor does, that California is the temple of the American Recovery. But you know, the hundreds of thousands of people who've left in the last couple of years don't seem to agree.\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: No. 750,000 people have left California in the last years. 352 businesses in the last four years. That is not a coincidence. That's causation.\par \par \uc2 Bad policy, high taxes, homelessness, you are tripping over people and their natural discharge as you try to make your way to school or to work or places of worship. And other man-made problems for \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , Shannon. The light rail that he said he was going to abandon, he turned -- changed his mind on that. Now, he's pumping billions more into it. It's not going to work.\par \par \uc2 And you mentioned San Francisco. The fact is Los Angeles also now has fentanyl surpassing meth as the number one crisis in drug overdose death. Oakland is completely destroyed. So, this isn't a fantasy or a concoction of the "right-wing."\par \par \uc2 We know that the left is failing in our major cities, including all across \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 's California because we have two eyes and two ears. It's very simple. One thing I want to say.\par \par \uc2 You can't blame Republicans when the eight top officeholders in the state of California are all elected Democrats. When Democrats control, if you added up the Senate and the assembly together, 96 seats to about 26 seats, Democrat and Republican. He owns all of this.\par \par \uc2 And all of the great things we love about California, the weather, the ocean, the beaches, the mountain, the -- has nothing to do with \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  and the Democrats. All the things we don't like about California, they have put in our footsteps.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well --\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: I think \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  should say mirror, mirror on the wall, who's got the most homeless of them all? And narcissists, the governor, will find the answer very plain and clear.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, I thought it was interesting that he said -- with right coming after him, he says they have to focus on our failures in order for them to be right. But, Greg, that seems to admit they do have failures.\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: First, I think it's really unfair of Kellyanne to wear that outfit. Because there are like 15 jokes I want to say, but I'm not going --\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: Don't.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I can't.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: Don't made me call -- (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Because I don't know her well enough. I'm afraid -- I'm as -- I'm afraid of Kellyanne Conway.\par \par \uc2 WILL CAIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Do one. Just one.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: You will be.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: It will be wonderfully awkward.\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: Super --\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Wait, am I going to have to call HR?\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: Superimpose Gavin's head on -- (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I would say Beetlejuice is looking for his jacket. But anyway, I'm joking. Look, he -- a couple of things -- or a lot -- a lot of things.\par \par \uc2 First of all, he called San Francisco resilient. You don't describe a place that's go -- doing really well as resilient. A very -- you describe a person who's undergoing serious health problems as they're really resilient.\par \par \uc2 So, this place is going through hell, hence, he calls it resilient. He brought up race, so you -- that opens the door to his policies, which are anti-black, anti-female, anti-Asian because all three of them are victims of his policies. You know, at least DeSantis's policies are about lifting all boats, not sinking all of them.\par \par \uc2 However, what is -- his point is irrelevant. Politicians point to each other's failures all the time, left and right. But that doesn't negate the failures.\par \par \uc2 We're going to talk about it later in the show. California is now going to be drinking water made out of feces, OK? That's not -- that's not a successful state.\par \par \uc2 Newsom's reasoning is that it's like blaming the guy who calls the fire department to put out a fire for the actual fire itself. His reasoning would blame anyone for making the 911 call to report a crime for simply calling out of concern and saying something. He would prefer that you do not say something, remain silent, lie back, and enjoy it.\par \par \uc2 You know, I was born and raised in California. It's not a political thing for me. It's a tragedy to see what's happening to the country -- to the state, and in effect to the country.\par \par \uc2 I would like to help. I'm not there just to point fingers. I saw firsthand experience here in NYC at the crime wave. We pointed this out on the show, I don't know, three years ago. We were the canaries in the coal mine here on THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 We were mocked by people on the -- on CNN who are no longer employed. Was that our fault for calling this out? We were called hysterics for pleading with Democrats to do something. If they listened years ago, they would have been heroes, and we would have been happy for them. And that's another point here.\par \par \uc2 You know, Republicans actually do want to help. They're not just pointing fingers, right? The weird thing about conservatives is they'll pull over and help fix your car or change a flat even if you got a Biden-Harris sticker on it.\par \par \uc2 It's part of being for small government, you know, relying on your -- on your neighbors and individuals. The model -- motto