e strongest Biden-Harris surrogates out there. And I think the fact that he took on that debate with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and stood up there and said, you should be talking to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , right? You're standing here with me, someone who's not on the ticket, and he'll be on in 2028. I'm sure that he'll get into the primary then.\par \par \uc2 But I don't think that he has an aspiration to do it right now. Frankly, I think that having just come out of COVID and the scenes that we see that California is not going to be ready. It's not the best laboratory to go out and run a presidential campaign on at this particular moment.\par \par \uc2 It doesn't mean that there haven't been strides in the right direction. We see pictures of homeless people all the time. The homeless rates are down in California, though.\par \par \uc2 10 percent of the jobs that were gained just last month in the U.S. came from California. And he's making a very valid point. Republicans -- and, Greg, you might be right that the average Republican is desperate to change my tire. And I would welcome it if I got a flat because I don't know what to do under those circumstances.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , stood up there and held a big poop map right, and didn't want to talk about the fact that Jacksonville has a 67 percent higher murder rate than San Francisco, right? He doesn't want to talk about the homelessness problem in Tampa. You talk about having to step over people, you got to do that in Tampa, too.\par \par \uc2 I have seen no politician of either party that stands up there and wants to olive branch with the other side and say, you know what you're doing? This right. Especially in a debate or when you have a friendly interview, you're going to take every opportunity to pound the other guy.\par \par \uc2 And they're clearly targeting DeSantis because if it's not Trump, he's quite formidable. I know Nikki Haley is pulling ahead of him in the head- to-head with Biden. B