s\uc2  gunman murdered three Israelis. And "BREAKING TONIGHT", Mike, we're learning that a fourth Israeli has died from friendly fire as a result of that attack.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 ANTONY BLINKEN\uc2 , UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF STATE: My heart goes out to the victims of this attack.\par \par \uc2 FOY (voice over): Four Israelis are dead, after two \uc2 Hamas\uc2  gunman opened fire in Jerusalem this morning, as Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  met with Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BENJAMIN NETANYAHU\uc2 , PRIME MINISTER, ISRAEL (through translator): I told him we swear and I swear to eliminate \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Nothing will stop us.\par \par \uc2 FOY (voice over): Blinken then met with \uc2 Mahmoud Abbas\uc2  of the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2 , discussing ways to accelerate humanitarian aid into Gaza, and improve security for Palestinians in the West Bank.\par \par \uc2 This mother is weeping tears of joy, finally reunited with her daughter. 21-year-old Mia Schem released by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists today, with 40-year-old Amit Soussana, and six other Israeli hostages.\par \par \uc2 But the joy of coming home can quickly turn into grief. On her first day back in Israel. American Israeli mother Liat Beinin learned \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorist murdered her husband on October 7th. She'll raise their three children alone.\par \par \uc2 But Israel is united against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and ready for whenever this ceasefire ends.\par \par \uc2 YOAV GALLANT, MINISTER OF DEFENSE, ISRAEL: We are going to fight \uc2 Hamas\uc2  until we prevail, no matter how long it takes.\par \par \uc2 FOY (voice over): Knowing whatever comes next in Gaza will be scrutinized by the international community.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 FOY: Secretary Blinken said tonight that Israel must take steps to protect the innocent civilians in Gaza, whenever the fighting does resume. Tomorrow is the eighth consecutive day of the temporary ceasefire. Mike?\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Nate Foy, live in northern Israel. Nate, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Questions continue to swirl concerning just how far President Biden's willing to go in his support of Israel. Congressional Republicans are demanding attention be paid to the southern border with Mexico, in order to get the President's funding request approved.\par \par \uc2 This comes into the president's diplomatic chief delivers a message to the Israelis.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Peter Doocy has details tonight. Good evening, Peter.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Mike, this is the first week since October 7th that President Biden's comments and activities about Israel are almost entirely behind the scenes. Nothing really on camera, including today at a meeting in the Oval Office with the president of Angola.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): America's top diplomat in Tel Aviv, imploring Israel not to sink to \uc2 Hamas\uc2 ' level whenever fighting resumes.\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN: It's imperative that Israel act in accordance with international humanitarian law and the laws of war. Even when confronting a terrorist group that respects neither.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): Officials at the White House are confirming details of a Biden-Netanyahu call, urging against a repeat of the offensive in Gaza's north.\par \par \uc2 REAR ADM. JOHN KIRBY (RET.), COORDINATOR FOR STRATEGIC COMMUNICATIONS, NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL: We do not support a move to the south, unless or until they have adequately accounted for the protection of innocent human life.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): Netanyahu reportedly told Biden, Israeli forces need to operate in the south to root out \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Biden's team is hopeful the ceasefire will continue --\par \par \uc2 KIRBY: One of the chances of an extension, and I just can't tell you that right now.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): But not forever.\par \par \uc2 KIRBY: We do not support a permanent ceasefire at this time.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): Biden's team is also urging Congress to hurry up and cut them a check to fund military operations in Ukraine and Israel.\par \par \uc2 KIRBY: The reason why it's a supplemental is because they are all urgent.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): Time is limited before the Senate is set to adjourn.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MITCH MCCONNELL (R-KY): Senate has two weeks.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: And Republicans are open to the new spending as long as they get money for the border.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): Republicans don't work with us in a bipartisan way on the border. Passing a supplemental is going to be very difficult.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (voice over): If Congress doesn't act by the end of this year, the White House worries they can't help Ukraine anymore.\par \par \uc2 KIRBY: President Putin appears certainly intent on continuing this conflict, and on taking it directly to the Ukrainian people. Again, at the coldest months of the year.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: President Biden hasn't said much of anything about Ukraine money, since \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  phoned him to say, there is not going to be any without those funds for the border.\par \par \uc2 The president and the first lady right now are on the south side of the White House at The Ellipse for a tree lighting for that National Christmas Tree that at this hour, two days ago, was laying flat after a 40-mile-an- hour gust of wind, but it has since been uprighted. Mike?\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Much better now. Peter Doocy, live in the North Lawn. Peter, thanks a lot.\par \par \uc2 One of the ironies of the Israel \uc2 Hamas\uc2  conflict is that groups supporting gender equality in the U.S. and abroad have been uncharacteristically silent about the terror groups use of rape against Israeli citizens.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Gillian Turner looks at