here were 14 attacks against U.S. troops in Iraq and nine in Syria in the past two weeks, not including today's attack.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. military does not count rocket attacks on its bases and outposts that land more than a mile from those bases, which is true of many of these attacks.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAKE SULLIVAN, U.S. NATIONAL SECURITY ADVISER: If American troops are attacked by Iran and its proxies, we will respond. We did respond. If attacks continue, we will respond. And I think the Iranians understand our message.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GRIFFIN: There have been three attacks on U.S. bases by Iranian proxy forces since the U.S. F-15 and F-16 strike on those weapons warehouses on the border with Iraq in Eastern Syria last Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 The failed drone strike on a U.S. base this weekend in Northeast Syria did not cause any casualties and caused no damage to the base infrastructure. In fact, the Iranian proxy drone landed in an open field, posing no threat to the Al-Shadadi Base in Hasakah.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Central Command has deployed the 26th Marine Expeditionary Unit to assist in the event of any evacuations of embassies or Americans in the region. Those Marines will be on board the USS Bataan, an amphibious assault ship currently in the Red Sea.\par \par \uc2 And, right now, \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 's leader, \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 , is keeping his rocket and anti-tank attacks below the radar, enough to avoid a massive response, I'm told. The USS Eisenhower, an aircraft carrier strike group, has entered the Mediterranean, having passed through the Strait of Gibraltar.\par \par \uc2 It is steaming toward the Persian Gulf, Sandra, and there are about 900 U.S. troops in Syria keeping ISIS at bay and 2,500 U.S. troops inside Iraq. They are all in danger as these Iranian proxies continue to try to test U.S. resolve with these ongoing attacks against U.S. bases -- Sandra.\par \par \uc2 SMIT