 as Jennifer just reported, from the Al Asad Air Base in Iraq. It did cause no injuries to any U.S. or coalition forces or damage to the base.\par \par \uc2 But, again, this is the 24th attack on U.S. forces in Iraq and Syria since October 17. These were not deemed a real threat to U.S. forces because of the proximity in which they landed. But how should we respond based on the information we have here?\par \par \uc2 MORAN: We should see a much more aggressive response by the Biden administration. By -- perhaps by just by chance, they didn't land where they were intended to land.\par \par \uc2 But there is no question but what -- Iran is attempting to distract the United States, to have us pay a price. And all of this, our support in -- our interest in supporting Israel is enhanced by our ability to push back on Iran for things they're doing to the United States and our interests around the globe.\par \par \uc2 And, in my view, it's not an unusual thing, it's not just a happenstance that we have Ukraine, China, Russia, and Israel, and now all these proxies funded and trained by Iran taking what's more than potshots at the United States of America. It requires a definite and firm response, not just words.\par \par \uc2 It's a serious circumstance.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Senator, what do you think about this plan that Speaker Johnson, the newly elected Speaker Johnson, has unveiled, $14.3 billion Israel aid package with cuts to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  to pay for it? What do you think?\par \par \uc2 MORAN: Well, I have called for hearings in the Appropriations Committee, which is going to take place. I'm a member of the Appropriations Committee, a defense appropriator, an appropriator for our intelligence services.\par \par \uc2 And we face tremendous challenges around the globe, Russia and Ukraine, China, and Taiwan, now Iran, the attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Israel. The clouds, those dark clouds are aligning. And we need to -- the reason for the hearing is to find out how that money is going to be spent. We're not going to just approve something the administration sends to Congress.\par \par \uc2 We need to use a fine-tooth comb and find out how best to spend the money to defend our allies, but, importantly, to make sure that the United States and our citizens are more secure as that money's spent. When we spend that money, we want to know that we're getting our money's worth in defending the American people.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Senator, we will see how all of that goes.\par \par \uc2 Could you weigh in on this moment that we are seeing happen here in the United States, this rise in antisemitism? The White House addressed it a short time ago, confirming that senior administration officials are agreeing now to meet with Jewish leaders in universities at American campuses to discuss what is happening at American college and universities in the wake of all of this.\par \par \uc2 Are you surprised by this? And what should be done to hold these people accountable?\par \par \uc2 MORAN: I would say I'm disappointed, as compared to surprise.\par \par \uc2 Antisemitism has been on the rise around the globe and here in the United States for the last several years. It's something that we would not expect because of who we are as Americans. We are not, we should not be capable of reaching these conclusions by stereotyping and attacking people based upon their heritage and religious views.\par \par \uc2 This is a sad day, and we certainly need to make certain that our universities are teaching and giving opportunities for certainly free speech, but teaching the truth, teaching the real story behind the history of countries, including Israel, around the globe.\par \par \uc2 So, terribly discouraging, terribly disappointing, and something that I would wish that would never happen here in the United States or any place on the globe.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Yes, and you look at those crowds that assembled there at that Russian airport as a flight was landing from Tel Aviv, the White House reacting to that today, calling it a chilling demonstration of hate, bigotry and intimidation.\par \par \uc2 I have got about 10 seconds left, sir.\par \par \uc2 MORAN: I would just say that I would not be surprised to learn that those are orchestrated efforts outside the United States to stir the world in anger against Israel at a time in which they're under attack, at a time in which the United States needs to be strong in support of Israel.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Senator, appreciate you joining us. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 MORAN: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: All right.\par \par \uc2 Neil will be back tomorrow. Florida Governor and Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  will join him.\par \par \uc2 And you can catch me weekdays 1:00 p.m. Eastern time alongside John Roberts on "America Reports" right here on the FOX News Channel.\par \par \uc2 "The Five" starts right now.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020231030ejau00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  Warns Iran Not To Attack American Troops; National Student Walkout To "End Siege On Gaza"; Bowman Charged For Pulling Capitol Fire Alarm; \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  Travels To China For Climate Talks; Can They Be Donated? Chris Pratt Sparks Childhood Trophy Debate; I Play For The Saints, Man: NFL Star Tres To Weasel Way Out Of Speeding Arrest\b0\pa