nce had over TikTok, which was absurd at the time for anyone following this, but now is proven to be a lie.\par \par \uc2 TikTok is controlled by ByteDance. And ByteDance is, of course, controlled by the Chinese Communist Party. So, therefore, we cannot allow the CCP to control the dominant media platform in America.\par \par \uc2 Yet, Congress has been silent on this issue and paralyzed for months now because of a massive lobbying campaign, multimillion dollar lobbying campaign on behalf of TikTok. They're weaponizing the D.C. swamp against us, but we have to act before it's too late.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, a bombshell report -- speaking of China, just came out from Politico. The CCP nabbed 60,000 emails from the State Department. We knew there was a hack, but we didn't know how pervasive it was. Among the most sensitive information stolen were victims' travel itineraries and diplomatic deliberations.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, we can't even secure our email in our government. What's our federal budget now for the State Department? What's their I.T. budget? We even know?\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yeah, it's massive. But here's what makes it even worse. Remember, we had the previous report that the Commerce Secretary's emails were hacked. And what did she do after that report? She went to Beijing to engage with the Chinese Communist Party.\par \par \uc2 So, despite the fact that the CCP has not relaxed its relentless economic and cyber warfare campaign against us, the Biden administration is trying to revive economic and diplomatic engagement with China as the foundation of our foreign policy. It's naive, it's dangerous, because we slow key defensive action that we need to take to defend ourselves.\par \par \uc2 And so, China's not slowing down, but we're slowing down because of some mistaken assumptions we have about the nature of this country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're going to have you back to talk about what's happening with Ford and the auto industry,