r likely tomorrow night just coming from the debate stage right over the Hill. You know, as we continue to see those extreme policies, we stand here rooted in the values that we know continue to ensure that we are growing our economy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. Rob, I'm not sure what values the Biden administration is rooted in. But She doesn't even seem to believe that. I mean, you're watching her body language. Listen, does she seem like she's really on board the Biden train or whatever we're calling it, caboose of Biden?\par \par \uc2 SCHNEIDER: I think it spoke volumes, the four supporters she was able to get at that press conference. I think that some of the values that the Biden administration, you know, wants to make sure, like what stoves we use, what kind of cars we drive, and what air conditioners we're allowed to have in our homes. These are the values of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 And I think it should be pretty much a slam dunk. You know, it's incredible, like, for me to see the defense for the Democrats is like, yes, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's son did take advantage of his father's position, but Joe didn't make any money off it.\par \par \uc2 Now, that's your defense? That's an admission of guilt. How is this still happening?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Rob, what's amazing about this is, well, you're from the field of comedy, obviously, and acting. Now, if this had been a Republican who had as many gaffes and as many physical stumbles and senior moments as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has had, I mean, this would be 24-7 on all the comedy sites, obviously, SNL. But with Biden, it's kind of, aw, shucks, ain't that cute or that's just Joe. But I mean, it's ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 SCHNEIDER: It's almost as if 95 percent of the media is in the hands of the illiberal liberal intelligentsia, and there's nothing we could do about it. No, they're going to -- the thing is about it, it's like their wrongs and their evil is going to be way -- way not as bad as ours as the conservatives. And they're just going to run with it.\par \par \uc2 And so, unfortunately, you really do have -- like I said before, I mean, people in California would vote for an avocado if it had a D next to it. And there's just a tribalism that I think people are waking up to.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I want you to moderate the next debate or the next debate.\par \par \uc2 SCHNEIDER: I'm there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: One of them. I'll pay to see that. I'll co-moderate with you. Rob, great to see you as always. Thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 SCHNEIDER: Thank you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, that was fun. Well, breaking news, just moments ago, the Senate just reinstated its dress code. Oh, I feel terrible for \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . What is he going to do now? Well, it felt good, comfortable. He just needed to breathe a little bit in that.\par \par \uc2 I mean, I'm trying to get my kids not to wear hoodies, and we couldn't get him. Well, who said bipartisanship is dead, OK? Now kids looking from the gallery, on high, they can look down and see everyone looking decently.\par \par \uc2 And look at all those people at the Reagan Library. They're all going to look great. All right, that's a good news, so dress code, little, little, little steps. Baby steps.\par \par \uc2 Don't forget, set your DVR so you always stay connected with us. Make sure to follow me on social media. Thanks for watching. Remember, it's America now and forever. Something I never get to do now, Jesse Watters takes it all from here. And Jesse, you always had a dress code in your studio, always.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS HOST: I did. It's jacket and tie only. But I'm really looking forward to the debate moderated by Ingram and Schneider.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Come on, Jess, come on. All right, we'll be watching you. Take it away.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020230928ej9r00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Joins UAW Strikers On Picket Line\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Sara Carter, Tomi Lahren, Jason Chaffetz, Dana  Perino, Gianno Caldwell \par \uc2 8,107 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2023\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to "Hannity".\par \par \uc2 And tonight, new bombshell allegations surrounding the Biden family syndicate. John Solomon is here with new details tonight.\par \par \uc2 Also, thanks to Joe, a new border town has emerged Chicago, Illinois, thousands of illegal immigrants stream into the Windy City. Its residents are already reeling from a crime crisis that continues to spiral. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GIANNO CALDWELL, FOX NEWS POLITICAL ANALYST: My brother Christian had the potential to do well in life, but Christian will never have the opportunity to go to college.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Our friend, Gianno Caldwell, he'll join us in a moment with more.\par \par \uc2 Now, first, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line in Michigan earlier today, at least pretending to show his support behind striking auto workers. They're demanding a large pay increase to keep up with rampant inflation caused by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . They're also asking for a 32-hour work week, something Biden could definitely get behind since he only works a few hours a week.\par \par \uc2 Joe reportedly now wakes up late, goes to bed early, spends almost all of his weekends resting and relaxing in Delaware, and he's taken more days off than any president in history. And your 80-year-old commander-in-chief just doesn't have the energy, the stamina to deal with the rigors of a traditional presidential schedule. It should be the toughest job in the world.\par \par \uc2 Is he up to it? I'm not sure he could be a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  greeter.\par \par \uc2 And now, another growing concern for the Biden White House, that would be his mobility. Look at this report from Axios. There is a critical new mission for Biden's staffers, operation don't let Joe fall again.\par \par \uc2 Given his frail condition, the president could be just one trip away from becoming seriously injured or worse, it could also mean politically his demise. Now, even if Biden survives a fall without injury, that might still confirm voters' very real, very deep concerns about his age, his physical strength, his cognitive abilities, because they're obvious in decline. We're watching it in real time.\par \par \uc2 According to "Axios", quote, Biden's team is taking extra steps to prevent him from stumbling in public as he did in June. Remember, why is he even has a hard time getting up there? When he tripped over a sandbag at the \uc2 Air Force Academy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, these steps include regular physical therapy now for the president, a new slip resistant tennis shoes and, of course, say bye, bye to the regular steps on Air Force One. Biden's mobility issues have become so bad had that he now relies on the short steps that's the -- a lower deck on the plane. It's easier to walk up those in the big steps.\par \par \uc2 Anyway pretty soon, I guess even those steps might become more than the president can handle. And you got it, right after they launched this operation, right there Joey slips and loses his footing, thank goodness he didn't fall, almost slid down the steps while deplaning. Not a great start for operation keep Joe from ever falling again.\par \par \uc2 Officially, the White House says Biden struggles with balance or related to arthritis, but given his history with brain aneurysms -- yeah, many experts and just common sense Americans are more than worried that a degenerative mental condition might very well be to blame, especially given Joe's struggle with language and short-term memory. Listen to Biden describe an initiative to bolster the U.S. Pacific Island partnership, an important alliance given China's aggression. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Strong growth begins with a strong infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 So today, I'm pleased to announce we're working with Congress to address $40 billion in our Pacific Islands infrastructure initiative. Recall the PGPI -- anyways, it doesn't matter what we call it but that's what it is. I was going to get back to acronyms, and I'm going to -- I'm going to withstand not doing that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why bother remembering an acronym. Who cares what we call it?\par \par \uc2 Whatever your politics, most rational Americans can honestly agree that you president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lacks the mental acuity to be an effective president. Would you hire him to be a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  greeter?\par \par \uc2 And it's only getting worse, but for some reason, Joe is running for reelection. Why? Honestly, who thinks that is a good idea?\par \par \uc2 According to an NBC News poll, look at this, two-thirds of Democratic voters, they want somebody other than Biden to run. These are unprecedented numbers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in deep trouble.\par \par \uc2 So, naturally, he turned to world-renowned loser \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  for advice. She reportedly is warning him to, quote, take seriously the possibility of third party candidates and they've siphoning all votes. Now, she should probably also tell Joe about Wisconsin. She forgot to visit that state in 2016, something maybe deep down inside she deeply regrets as she continued her -- continues her election denialism by saying they're going to do it again. Trump is going to work with Russia again.\par \par \uc2 The only one that worked with Russia is her, with her dirty Russia misinformation dossier she paid for.\par \par \uc2 Now so far, Joe has been hit hard by liberals that I never thought we'd really see attacking a Democratic president. Maureen Dowd, David Ignatius, even liberal Joe, David Axelrod, Van Jones, James Carville, and then Carville hit him again when he went on Bill Maher's podcast and hit him even harder.\par \par \uc2 Now, unfortunately, for Democrats, Joe is ignoring all the advice and at this point he can barely keep up with his day job, much less non-stop action of a campaign, aside of course from the few rare appearances away from the East Coast and a couple of private fundraisers and when he's at the fundraisers, now we have reports that he tells a story, and a few minutes later to the same group tells the story again. What is that a sign of? Those not really campaigning. He'll be in the basement bunker soon enough.\par \par \uc2 Now, despite all the bad polls, he's treating his re-election campaign like a coronation. Even today's photo op at the \uc2 UAW\uc2  picket line lasted all of 15 minutes, including a five-minute speech. Let's be clear, he doesn't care what is happening in these negotiations.\par \par \uc2 That was just a show appearance. He only showed up because Joe is hemorrhaging support among union workers and frankly for good reason. If his radical green new deal policies take hold, many of their jobs will be lost.\par \par \uc2 Electric vehicles means less \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers are needed. And between the environmental regulations, new corporate taxes, the electric vehicle quotas, union staff factories in Michigan will be unaffordable -- all the remaining jobs will be exported or automated.\par \par \uc2 This is another inconvenient truth for Democrats and unions. Middle class Joe has always been and continues to be a farce. He might be at the picket line today but he sides with the elitists, the climate alarmist religious cult members, a hundred percent of the time.\par \par \uc2 And despite their humble roots, both Joe and Dr. Jill Biden, they're disgusted by the middle class. They are long-time social climbers who will do whatever it takes to fit in with the blue bloods of Washington, D.C. They want to be invited to the parties.\par \par \uc2 And today's elites, they just care more about their climate alarmism, lacking in science than good paying American jobs.\par \par \uc2 And meanwhile, what would \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  do? Well, he actually helped the \uc2 UAW\uc2  out and helped them keep their great career-paying jobs by hitting China like he did before with massive tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, joining us now from Michigan with a full report from Biden's brief appearance at the picket line, Sara Carter joins us tonight -- Sara.\par \par \uc2 SARA CARTER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Hey, Sean, yes. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  -- president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spent a whopping like 12 minutes with those -- with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  workers outside the plant today. And I can tell you that the time I spent with hundreds of workers walking up and down that line, it was stunning to see how they had turned on the administration.\par \par \uc2 None of them actually bought the visit. They said that they were concerned it was more political than it was supportive, and they had a lot to say.\par \par \uc2 Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Do you think President Biden's arrival here in Michigan today is a show of support or a show of politics?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: That's all about votes, trying to get votes.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Do you feel like him showing up right now is -- is a show or is it a show?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's a show to me.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I mean, that's just to help the EV economy, not the gas economy, okay?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you think that we want to buy EVs because it keeps their (ph) jobs.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Right.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You know?\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Right and it's -- and for a lot of people, it's just too expensive.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: And that has been the big deal and --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You can't even afford the products we make now, and that's a big problem.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Do you trust this show of support coming from Washington right now? Do you think it's going to mean something in the end?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I could all I could do is hope that it does. I mean, it's just -- all of this that's happening -- everything from the president coming out, from everyone coming out to support, it's all in hopes that we can see some kind of change.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: You feel like the American worker is being ignored?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They didn't forget us during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Right.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Because we during the pandemic, we was building cars.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Right. We was working.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Right.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARTER: Sean, they say the White House has pushed and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has pushed for this green agenda with electric vehicles is actually pushing them out of the workforce. And they say they won't stand for it. Inflation is high and they're wondering what's next. They're going to continue to picket.\par \par \uc2 And as they continue to picket and as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  got into his vehicle, he headed straight back to his plane, on to California to Silicon Valley for a fundraiser -- Sean.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Sara Carter, great reporting as always. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with more is the host of "Tomi Lahren is Fearless" on Outkick, Tomi Lahren and former senior advisor to President Trump, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All right. So, Tomi, we begin with operation keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from falling on his face didn't actually have a great first day because he nearly fell on his face again going down the shorter stairs of Air Force One. You really can't make that up, can you?\par \par \uc2 TOMI LAHREN, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: No and it's pretty sad that we're at this point now that we're worried that the leader of the free world can get on and off stairs, even the smaller stairs without incident or accident. But you have to wonder what the rest of the world is thinking. You know, our enemies are waiting to pounce and they see this man who can't even take the kitty stairs.\par \par \uc2 And if there's ever a time to pounce, now would be the time and there's no coincidence that you've got tens of thousands of people coming across our border each and every single week, they see this man that can't mountain and get up the stairs on his own and they know that this is the time for them to take over America, to come for everything that we have.\par \par \uc2 Our enemies see it. Putin sees it. Of course, the ayatollahs see it. The world sees it and how embarrassing that this has to be their primary focus.\par \par \uc2 Let's just make sure that our president doesn't fall down today, also because the vice president could be potentially even worse. That's where the Democrat Party is.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , he's loving this more than anybody else, I have a feeling.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I think so, but he swears up and down, left and right, that he's not running under any circumstances.\par \par \uc2 All right. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , as I -- as I look at all this today, you know, he goes to label the acronym -- oh it doesn't matter what we call it, because he couldn't remember it. They have nearly fall on the first day of operation don't let Biden fall again.\par \par \uc2 Then, of course, you know, you put that on top of what we learned last week. He bumps into a flagpole, doesn't shake the hand of his Brazilian counterpart to buy, wanders away, and, you know, it's like every single time he opens his mouth, even when it's not a disaster, it's mumbling, bumbling almost incoherent from him, it's obviously -- his cognitive issues are getting worse, and it's impacting his -- you know, physical health as well.\par \par \uc2 How do they stick with this guy?\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: Well, the pace of the decline is accelerating quickly, Sean. Let's not mince words. This is a horror show.\par \par \uc2 The White House placed a story today about operation don't let Joe trip where they're going to put him in comfy support sneakers and they're going to have him go up the little staircase, the back entrance to Air Force One and the man still nearly toppled down a flight of stairs in the view of the entire world. He cannot put two sentences coherently together. As you say, he's mumbling and bumbling and stumbling.\par \par \uc2 Not to mention this whole trip which was clearly a response to President Trump going down to speak to the auto workers is completely nonsensical, because they're protesting \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's policy, Sean.\par \par \uc2 It's his climate policies. It's his energy mandates. It's his trade policies, his inflation, his bad economy that is driving down wages and living conditions and employment opportunities for auto workers.\par \par \uc2 So we have a president that can't speak, can't talk, can't walk, can't move and his economic policies are leading to ruin nation for America's working and middle class.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, what -- it was reported -- we don't have it on tape, Tomi, but it was reported -- it was widely reported about this incident when he was with -- you know, a group of, you know, doing a fundraiser group of supporters, financial supporters.\par \par \uc2 So I don't know if you've ever met anybody that has dementia, even early onset, or Alzheimer's. Look, it's sad, it's tragic. I've seen it up front, up close and personal, you don't wish that on anybody.\par \par \uc2 But with that said is one of the classic symptoms of this type of cognitive decline is what happened at this private meeting where he told the story, you know, and then a few minutes later, not remembering that he just told the story told it again. You know, another characteristic would be -- you know, people ask you a question, you give them an answer and a few minutes later, they'll ask you the question again. And 10 minutes after that, they might even ask at another time -- very classic symptoms that are now, you know, beginning to become very public.\par \par \uc2 So, I mean, we can only imagine the shape he's going to be in, you know, a year from now.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: They can't hide this much longer, Sean, and they know that, and that's why there's a panic mode going on right now with the DNC because they know they have to get rid of Joe. They're not really worried about that. I don't think that they worry too much about pushing him off to the side. They worry what they're going to do about their Kamala situation.\par \par \uc2 They can get Joe out of the way but how do they get over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ? How do they install \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is quite frankly their worst nightmare? So I think it's interesting.\par \par \uc2 Gavin swears up and down that he's not running, but you have to listen to the way that he says that. He's not going to run against Joe but it's not as if he's not going to be the replacement for Joe. So the way that he discusses this, I hang on every single word that he says.\par \par \uc2 So make no mistake, the Democrats -- they're done with Joe, they're tired of Joe, they can't hide this much longer but they got to figure out their Kamala situation and that's where they have the hang up because they push the identity politics and they don't know how to leapfrog her with the white man from California with the good hair.\par \par \uc2 That's a hard sell to the party that has been built around identity politics.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Last word, Steve Miller.\par \par \uc2 LAHREN: That's their challenge, best of luck.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah, last word, Steve.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Yes they're -- they're in an impossible situation and they have no way out. They can't get around the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  problem because they have lived by identity politics. They've made that their highest order so they can't go around her to get to \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , but they can't get rid of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, ultimately, it's going to be a total train wreck. Plus, they have RFK Jr. who maybe will run as a third party. They don't know what to do. But my advice to Republicans is keep your eye on the ball, keep these investigations going, do not relent, do not stop until all the facts are uncovered.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Okay and it's Cornel West, it's RFK Jr., maybe he's talking to the libertarian party, then you got the No Labels party. That's a lot of potential third party competition.\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you both. Thank you, Tomi. Thank you, Steve Miller.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  is now suing former New York City Mayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . We'll explain why and a growing number of Democrats now calling for Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  to resign. They don't seem to care about the Biden scandals, you know, Menendez is less than a million dollars.\par \par \uc2 Eighteen Democrats want him out. Are they paying attention to the tens and tens of millions of dollars of the Biden syndicate? Anyway, we'll go through that straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Another day, another troubling development for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . Now, according to new reports, the White House and House Ways and Means Committee, well, they are preparing to release even more sensitive information about this investigation into the troubled first son.\par \par \uc2 Now, meanwhile earlier today zero experienced Hunter, he actually filed a lawsuit against former New York City Mayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , resorting to the left's favorite talking point, accusing him of hacking his laptop from hell., Remember he said in the beginning, I have no idea if that's my laptop.\par \par \uc2 Now, according to breaking report from justthenews.com and photos, they show the former U.S. ambassador to Ukraine, remember her name during the Ukrainian impeachment, Maria Yovanovitch? Remember her? Well, she apparently met twice with a barista official after being told that the firm was allegedly corrupt.\par \par \uc2 Now, Just The News founder John Solomon, he joins us with more, investigative reporter, editor-in-chief.\par \par \uc2 Sir, how are you?\par \par \uc2 JOHN SOLOMON, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, JUSTTHENEWS.COM: Good to be with you. Yeah, good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, we -- remember that name. That's a blast from the past, but here's the interesting part of this, John. You know, she was kind of sanctimonious about the whole issue of Trump's impeachment, so she's warned that this company's corrupt, and yet still meets with company executives. Explain that one.\par \par \uc2 SOLOMON: Yeah. We'll take everybody back to the 2019 time frame. First off, she was the ambassador who ordered her staff to monitor yours and mine and other conservatives' social media that was raising questions about \uc2 Burisma\uc2 . That's an issue that's been out there.\par \par \uc2 During the impeachment proceedings against President Trump, she said she really didn't know anything about \uc2 Burisma\uc2  except what she learned in her first briefing and what she read in the newspaper. We later learned that she got several briefings, one of them from one of the lawyers representing \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , another, a face-to-face meeting with one of \uc2 Burisma\uc2 's blue star strategy lobbyists who were trying to lobby the State Department to drop the corruption story about \uc2 Burisma\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now, we know in 2017, the first year that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president, she had not one but two meetings with Vadim Pojarski. Now if that name sounds familiar, that's the \uc2 Burisma\uc2  official that most regularly dealt with \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , instead of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's handler while \uc2 Burisma\uc2  was paying \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  all those millions of dollars. He'd got on not one but two stages with the ambassador official events. I think they were at the U.S. Ukraine Chamber of Commerce or business council, and there, a man representing a company that the State Department repeatedly said, we don't want to deal with, he's corrupt, don't go near him.\par \par \uc2 In fact, Maria Yovanovitch once sent an email to \uc2 John McCain\uc2  staff saying, don't go near \uc2 Burisma\uc2 , she has not one but two meetings in 2017. The only reason we didn't find out about these meetings back during the 2019 impeachment, these photos, these web posts were deleted. We were alerted to them by a State Department official who remembered them and we found them in the Internet archives.\par \par \uc