ng in the House. And so are Republicans and Democrats, unfortunately, in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 So the House Republicans are the only thing standing between that. But we have got to have the resolve and the stomach to make the tough choices. We have got to stare down the Senate and the White House and say, no, we have got to cut our spending in the House. We're not going nearly far enough.\par \par \uc2 We're going to pass our spending bills, cutting our spending and reducing. We're going to cut some $60, $70 billion this year. But that's not nearly enough, as you know, Charles...\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Right.\par \par \uc2 GOOD: ... when you're running about a $200 billion monthly deficit.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: All right.\par \par \uc2 Representative, thank you very much. Appreciate you coming on.\par \par \uc2 And, folks, I want to get back to this breaking news following the indictment of Democrat Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 . Senate Majority Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  says that Menendez has decided to step down for now as chair of the Foreign Relations Committee.\par \par \uc2 We're going to get some reaction from Capitol Hill coming up.\par \par \uc2 Also, migrants at the border already topping last year's record high. Now new video shows more are on the way. We will get the latest.\par \par \uc2 Plus, it's looking like a weekend washout, as mini-Tropical Storm Ophelia closes in. For -- FOX -- FOX Weather, rather, coverage is coming right up.\par \par \uc2 We will be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Back to the breaking news, following the indictment of Democrat Senator \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chad Pergram is on Capitol Hill with more -- Chad.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Well, this morning, I indicated that it was a pretty clear situation that \uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2 , the chair of the Foreign Relations Committee, would step down temporarily.\par \par \uc2 And that's been made official just in the past couple of minutes here. We have a statement from \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the majority leader.\par \par \uc2 And he says: "\uc2 Bob Menendez\uc2  has been a dedicated public servant and is always fighting hard for the people of New Jersey. He has a right to a due process and a fair trial."\par \par \uc2 He says: "Senator Menendez has rightly decided to step down temporarily from his position as chairman of the Foreign Relations Committee until the matter is resolved."\par \par \uc2 Now, Charles, this mirrors what happened some years ago when he was indicted the first time and the Democrats were in the minority, and so Menendez was the ranking Democrat on the Foreign Relations Committee. He stepped aside at that point.\par \par \uc2 It's a Democratic Caucus rule that, if you're indicted for a felony, you cannot clasp a gavel in the Senate. So we don't know officially who will step in to chair that committee. When Menendez stepped aside some years ago during the first trial, Ben Cardin, the Democratic senator from Maryland, took that role -- Charles.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Chad, thank you very, very much.\par \par \uc2 All right folks, let's go back to the border, because new video shows migrants bound for the U.S. border traveling on top of another cargo train through Mexico, this as CBP is facing a record number of migrants already at the border.\par \par \uc2 FOX News Griff Jenkins is there with the latest -- Griff.\par \par \uc2 JENKINS: Hey, Charles. Good afternoon.\par \par \uc2 And there's literally no end inside. Let me just go straight to our flight drone team and show you just feet from where I'm standing another group of migrants trying to negotiate through the razor-sharp wire here along the banks, most of them telling us they're from Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 And most of them know that, when they are in the custody of Border Patrol, they will eventually be released with some sort of notice to appear at a court date years from now, and most won't show up. That's why this