e greatest political scandal of our lifetime.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, the country is watching, and we are as well to see where it goes.\par \par \uc2 I want to touch on something that's happening in your home state as well. A number of -- the issue of immigration. A number of House Democrats went over to one of the facilities where people are being housed, who have come here illegally. They were basically drowned out by protesters there.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , among one of them. She's not happy that the mayor there, Eric Adams, said this is basically potentially going to destroy the city.\par \par \uc2 She responded to him on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying this: the core issue is not solely the presence of asylum seekers. And there's a debate about whether all these people are asylum workers. But they want to work and New Yorkers want to hire them. The government is forcing people to remain on public systems because we won't let them work and support themselves. She says that's all they want.\par \par \uc2 So, would you favor work permits for people who are here and want to work, and are subsisting on government funding that, you know, Eric Adams says is now going to overwhelm the city? How would you deal with the immediate crisis?\par \par \uc2 STEFANIK: The immediate crisis is to secure the border, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 Let's take a step back. Mayor Adams and Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  support sanctuary city policies. There is a reason that New York is getting overrun and it's because of the border crisis and it's because of the illegal transfers of illegals into New York's state. They try to transfer these illegals to parts of Upstate New York, Upstate -- not only New York Republicans but Democrats as well, at the elected level spoke out strongly against this.\par \par \uc2 So, the way to solve this is by securing our border which is why House Republicans put a border security bill on the floor. We voted in