ican Americans. They live in the parks, in the subways, in the streets, many of them have emotionally disturbed issues. They get nothing. They have to show up at a shelter, there's a curfew. Illegal aliens is, there's no curfew. They get to smoke weed drink cerveza at taxpayers expense right up and down the streets, on motorbikes investments.\par \par \uc2 Where did they get the money for this? Americans are outraged, Democrats, Republicans and Independents. And AOC, she doesn't understand that because the princess is never out in the streets anymore. She's up in the streets suites getting wined dined in pocket lined.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: All right. Curtis, thanks for taking time with us this afternoon. We're going to leave it there.\par \par \uc2 SLIWA: This is just the beginning of many more actions to come. You watch.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: All right. Well, Democratic presidential candidate RFK Jr. now is fighting against his party's officials at the DNC accusing leadership of falling off track and creating an uneven playing field by outwardly favoring incumbent President Biden. Stick with us.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ROBERT F. KENNEDY JR. (D), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: We live in a time when a lot of people are having our belief system that is rigged, that democracy is no longer functioning and that the Democratic Party ought to be a template for democracy, and ought to be role modeling democracy. And we ought to have, you know, I think most Americans assume that the candidate illusion is the candidate who gets the most votes. And we should have rules that actually reflect that assumption.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Welcome back. Robert F. Kennedy Jr. now accusing the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  of "rigging the primaries to get President Biden reelected," that he's doing this by refusing he says to hold debates and making South Carolina the first contest ahead of Iowa and 