t we're going to do our due diligence. We're going to look for transparency and get accountability for the American people. We're not prejudging. We're just saying there's something really shady going on here. And the more dots that we're connecting, it's leading to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I don't know what to make of television coverage, Congresswoman, but I'm just wondering if these gun charges against the president's son have changed the complexion of the impeachment inquiry case, whatever you want to call it, when I notice all the networks were around the clock on this when it broke, including our two prominent rivals, that maybe this has changed that debate and made this impeachment inquiry, even though these were, to your earlier point, separate issues, more palatable.\par \par \uc2 I don't know any other way to describe it. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 MALLIOTAKIS: Well, the important thing for people -- the important thing for people to know is that these gun charges are unrelated to what the impeachment inquiry is about.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: True.\par \par \uc2 MALLIOTAKIS: We're talking about $20 million that came from entities that were created to funnel money to nine Biden family members.\par \par \uc2 That is completely different. That's influence peddling that we believe has taken place.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: But does this now -- you're quite right, but I'm just wondering, given the gravity and the attention this story has gotten on all the news networks, that this makes your case, even though a very different case, more acceptable? It even includes some of your more doubtful fellow Republican members.\par \par \uc2 I don't know if that applies to some of the Democratic members. What do you think?\par \par \uc2 MALLIOTAKIS: Well, look, it's up to us to make sure that we present the evidence to the American people and to our colleagues in Congress.\par \par \uc2 I will say that I believe that these charges have emerged simply because of what the Republicans have been doing in showing that the law enforcement entities in this administration have been treating the family of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  differently than the rest of the country.\par \par \uc2 So they had to do something to show that they're being serious. And this is it. But I think this is just, like I said, the tip of the iceberg.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman, thank you for taking the time. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 MALLIOTAKIS: All right.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, we have a lot more coming up, including how this is weighing on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 We will have \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  with us, the North Dakota governor -- after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: We are about seven-and-a-half-hours from about 146,000 autoworkers walking off the jobs at the Big Three automakers.\par \par \uc2 A deal or something to broker it is now running close to out of time -- after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, reaction on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 We have been hearing from the former president. A guy who wants to be the next president joins us right now, Republican North Dakota Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , kind enough to join us.\par \par \uc2 Governor, good to see you.\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 DOUG BURGUM\uc2  (R-ND), PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Neil, great to be with you as always.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: What do you make of this for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and the possibilities here that this changes things going forward?\par \par \uc2 BURGUM: Well, I think this is just the tip of the iceberg with these indictments.\par \par \uc2 The bigger issue is influence peddling and the fact that the president of the United States could be compromised on foreign policy with countries because of illegal payments channeled through these shell companies. But I think it's good that the inquiry is going on.\par \par \uc2 I think 