y.\par \par \uc2 The smoke forcing the \uc2 FAA\uc2  to shut down multiple airports during the day and Major League Baseball has postponed tonight's Yankees White Sox game due to the air quality, the city's mayor is warning vulnerable residents to stay inside.\par \par \uc2 ERIC ADAMS, MAYOR OF NEW YORK CITY: The New York is -- must take precaution. We recommend vulnerable New Yorkers stay inside. And all New Yorkers should limit outdoor activity to the greatest extent possible. This is not the day to train for a marathon or to do an outside event with your children. Stay inside, close windows and doors and use air purifiers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And while Americans choke on the smoke, the far left smells an opportunity. AOC thinks this is a great time to push her Green New Deal. She says that we must "Adapt our food systems, energy grids, infrastructure and healthcare to prepare for what's to come".\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats are pumping up climate hysteria and bringing back, you guessed it, mask insanity.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ADRIANO ESPAILLAT (D-NY): I wear my mask in solidarity. Climate change is not a hoax. We're not only seeing the haze from these fires, we're also feeling it in our very own lungs.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): The work to protect our climate is far from over. And we're dangerously behind.\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: Totally getting worse. But this is why the president has made climate change a priority. This is why he's taking the aggressive actions, that he's taken historic actions.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: So, what are our friends in doing about this? Their Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  is not issuing an apology. But he does seem worried about the kids.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN TRUDEAU\uc2 , CANADIAN PRIME MINISTER: People across the country are being 