2 If he's hurt and taken out of the game. We all know what Plan B is.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Greg, would you like to pounce on Biden fall?\par \par \uc2 GREG GUTFELD, FOX NEWS HOST: Oh, I'm so ready to pounce, but get this, I'm not going to pounce on his physical problems, right? Because that's what they want. Right?\par \par \uc2 This helps the Democrats to focus on the body and not the brain. He's actually in good physical shape. He's not fat, but his brain, his brain is in big trouble.\par \par \uc2 I would prefer a brain floating in a vat of nutrients at this point, believe in science, you know, small government and the right to personal safety.\par \par \uc2 So, he -- the horror -- the horrifying part about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , it has nothing to do with falling but failing. He's failing America in a radical departure from basically all of our American values. And that's either he's not interested in crime. He's not interested in education. He's not interested in protecting kids from activists, and probably the biggest assault that he's done in America is on the melting pot.\par \par \uc2 I mean, that's a that's a prime American value and he turned the dial up on the melting pot, but by embracing oppression politics, right?\par \par \uc2 He's now put a target on white saying that there's this huge villain, right? Extreme white MAGA extremist white supremacist, but they really can't find them.\par \par \uc2 But who knew that the face of like an anti-American revolution would be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's face? And it's because he's not there. He's just a husk. He's being used. He had -- he abdicated his own soul for the job.\par \par \uc2 So, I guess what I'm saying is, yes, he's a frail old man, and I'll make fun of him to the day he leaves about falling. If that gets him out, if that gets him out, great.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Whatever it takes.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Whatever it takes. But that's not the problem. The falling is not the problem. This is a dark and dreary path that we've selected in this man. That's the problem.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He has a mental problem and a physical problem. And all the voters have said that, two-thirds.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: I fell yesterday. So, that makes me an expert.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I actually pushed you.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: That's true.\par \par \uc2 KELLYANNE CONWAY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: The sandbags' fault. There's no question. The Washington Post ABC poll last month made that clear that two- thirds of voters including many Democrats say that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  lacks the mental sharpness and the physical agility to be president.\par \par \uc2 And to many voters, agility is ability. I agree with Greg, and I've been saying this for a very long time, let's not fall into the trap. The art of politics is to tell people not what they can see. But what they can't see.\par \par \uc2 When I think of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , I don't think the guy falling although it's odd. I don't think -- I don't think of the guy shaking hands with the air. As weird as that is.\par \par \uc2 I think of the guy who with no rationale, no plan, ignore the advice of all his generals and pull that out of Afghanistan like that, leaving $7.2 billion worth of our intelligence equipment for the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  to have.\par \par \uc2 And what's the point in this country of having the first female vice president -- first female vice president of color, if the women and Afghan are less free, have fewer rights, because her and her boss are so reckless with foreign policy?\par \par \uc2 Another point about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and that is going to matter to voters. And I'm not here to do the what-aboutism that it's Republicans to. When \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  falls, I think of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  falling us as the rest of the country. But the fear of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  being president again, and the fear of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  being president soon, makes many otherwise reasonable rational Democrats say and do crazy things. They defend what we can all see, which is a president who's not up to the job.\par \par \uc2 The founders in developing the United States Constitution said the president and the vice president must be 35 years of age and U.S. citizens, they assumed that those two people would be able to talk and walk properly.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: When the President falls, the first thing I think of is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Are Democrats -- does that cross their mind every time you see him stumble like that?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Well, every time something like that happened one time and there was a visible sandbag that the man tripped over. So, whether that's the advance team's fault. I mean, he was up there for two hours prior to that, so maybe they didn't think that he would be shifting back that way. Whoever you want to blame, people trip and like Greg tripping yesterday can no longer be president.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: No, of course not, I just don't --\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: -- fall in Wilmington.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: OK, if you want to -- let's take a trip through history of presidents falling. Let's start with \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , who was like the second coming of Jesus.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: He fell in love with Nancy.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: He fell on the steps of Air Force One.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Gerald Ford.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes. And we had -- I mentioned it yesterday, we had a president in a wheelchair, who everybody likes a lot, who revolutionized the country.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You're not making your point.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes, I --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, you're not because the Fed -- FDR was a Democrat. The only examples you're using that we remember are Republicans. You see my point?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Right. And you didn't pay any attention to it. You did not care about \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CONWAY: This is different.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD