: This weekend in Chicago, the latest 53 shot, 11 dead. You've got a Democratic mayor promising vowing to help this city. I mean, they're losing businesses, Jesse, you know, they're losing residents, people are fleeing the cities where violence is just such a huge issue.\par \par \uc2 But to Stephen A. Smith point about the black on -- black violence that is happening, why is nobody talking about it?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Well, the media is dominated by white liberals, most of the shows on cable or national T.V. are anchored by white liberals. And are white liberals comfortable talking about black-on-black crime? They're not. White liberals have not spent a lot of time in inner city communities. They don't have any cultural awareness. They don't have the news chops to report on thorny issues like drug trafficking, absent fathers, poor education systems, and they don't want to point out the fact that a lot of these cities have been run by Democrats for decades. And a lot of the democratic policies have not only not only helped, they've actually hurt these communities.\par \par \uc2 Plus, if you're a white liberal, and you're on T.V., you don't want to offend anybody. So, you want to be talking about black-on-black crime, and then say something that's going to get everybody upset. So they're very, very cautious.\par \par \uc2 You have, I don't know, \uc2 Joy Reid\uc2  and Don Lemon. They're black anchors, hold on, used to be, they still don't talk about black-on-black crime on their shows. No, they don't. Because we have producers monitoring what they do. They don't talk about it. And that is a huge tragedy and missed opportunity.\par \par \uc2 I don't know of their backgrounds, but Stephen A. Smith grew up really poor in Queens, really poor. Now he is the most successful sports personality in the country.\par \par \uc2 Maybe that's why he's able to talk about it because of his background. And that's why the liberal media should hire more people like Stephen A. Smith