\par \uc2 Nile, how do you think this is all going to go down?\par \par \uc2 NILE GARDINER, FORMER ADVISER TO BRITISH PRIME MINISTER: Well, thanks very much for having on the show, Neil.\par \par \uc2 I think the coronation is going to be a huge and massive success. The streets of London are absolutely full. You have literally, I think, hundreds of thousands, if not millions of people from around the world who are in London at the moment to attend or to really celebrate, I think, the coronation.\par \par \uc2 I have to say it's a very good thing, I think, that \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2  is not actually at the coronation. I think she would have been booed on the streets of London. So there's a very good reason why Meghan is not here. Harry is going to make a very quick exit. Apparently, within two hours of the main ceremony, he's heading back to California, which many have seen as very disrespectful here in London.\par \par \uc2 Also missing, of course, along with \uc2 Meghan Markle\uc2  is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Biden is absent from the coronation. I do think this is a very rude signal that Biden is sending to the British people, a lot of unhappiness certainly on the ground in the U.K. with regard to Biden not bothering to attend.\par \par \uc2 And Biden is seen by many Brits as very anti-British.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Really?\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Hilary, I'm wondering about how this is received among the British people.\par \par \uc2 You hear that King Charles is not thought of in the same way his mother was, that he's got to fight that back. But his poll ratings still seem pretty high.\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: How do they like him thus far?\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: Yes, a few points there to go with what Nile just said about the British feelings.\par \par \uc2 It's rather ironic, actually, because Biden is an English name. His ancestors emigrated from West Sussex in England.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Wow.\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: And yet he dwells on this Irish heritage. And it's because, when he was younger, he had a stutter, and his family, his mother made him memorize these Irish poems that were very anti-English.\par \par \uc2 So that's where I think that sentiment comes as a boy. That's number won. But also with regard to then the polls, yes, actually, if we all remember, right after his mother passed, Queen Elizabeth, I believe, ubiquitously, you heard and saw and the polls reflected that his speech right after she passed, every single tone of it was absolutely as it should have been.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Interesting.\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: And it was universally well-received.\par \par \uc2 So his poll numbers, yes, are good. The issue is, though, that the younger generation -- none of us sitting here right now are over 60. But those people that are over 60 are -- really think the world of him. And he's got over an 80 percent rating.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 FORDWICH: It's the younger under-35s that don't. That's the issue.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it. All right, guys, well, one of us is over 60, but I digress.It's always great seeing you.\par \par \uc2 Enjoy tomorrow, of course, FOX's coverage with Martha and everyone else. Of course, we will be picking up at the baton at 10:00 a.m., the implications of all of that.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, thank you for having fun with us about Adele.\par \par \uc2 And, Adele, all you have to do is call. Just call me.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may no