out relationships with their children.\par \par \uc2 Then you had George H.W. Bush, right? There was questions when the savings and loan crisis happened. Neil Bush, like, OK, we got to ask about that.\par \par \uc2 Remember, \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2  had a situation? The Clintons had a situation with a relative and the now their own situation.\par \par \uc2 So, it puts -- I think that what happens in this case with this particular one is that the staff is in a very difficult position, because President Biden wants his son defended. On some of these things, his son does not deserve to be defended.\par \par \uc2 And if you look back to some of the e-mails that we know that were happening in the Obama White House where they were e-mailing to each other saying, guys, have you seen, like, are you worried? I think I worried. We shouldn't -- I don't think Hunter -- what?\par \par \uc2 And they're nervous about it, but the president has never given them an off-ramp because he demands complete fealty to him and to Hunter.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, Jessica, what Dana is talking about is there is an e-mail, where to Schwerin who was the president of Rosemont Seneca that's now defunct. She's done everything she can to not use it. And they're referring to Kate Beddington telling -- Bedingfield to tell -- telling the Bloomberg people.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Yes. So, \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2  actually just left recently, and she's been in Biden world for ages. And when I read the e-mail exchange, you could sense her frustration coming off the page, right?\par \par \uc2 Like, this is not what I signed up for. Right? I signed up to work with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  . Everyone knows who he is, right? Someone who has this long reputation is getting things done. And this isn't their job. It's not \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  's job. That's why they got Ian Sams to do this.\par \par \uc2 And I think that to go beyond what Dana was saying about how President Biden wants his son defended. There's a disconnect between how serious he thinks the issue is and the reality of it, not necessarily because I think that this is a crime syndicate because I really don't think that.\par \par \uc2 But these are the --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Who paid you to say that?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: We get paid by the same person. Voters, Democrats are not going to not vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over this, unless a crime syndicate is proven. But it's the little annoying things such as bug you, where you're like, why do I have to deal with this? Right? Why are these stories coming out? And why is there no cohesive narrative against it?\par \par \uc2 And that's what Erin Burnett brought up on her show earlier in the week, which said, here's the layperson and you're looking at this, it's kind of stinky, right, what's happening here? And --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: What would the narrative be?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, if there was some declaration, where you don't even have to say my son is completely corrupt in any way, but just to say, I never personally profited from this because that's what -- people voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  . (INAUDIBLE) I don't know.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, it is not true. Well, I don't know, it seems like there are a lot of inconsistencies floating around from what Hunter has said versus what the president has maintained. And I hope that's because they don't record align each other.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: It's not -- it's not enough to say I didn't personally profit if your entire family is profiting.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: That's -- OK. So we all know --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You're at the center of it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: We all know about nepotism, right? I don't need to do the Schoolhouse Rock about that. There are a lot of very powerful families were brothers and sisters --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But this is China.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: So what?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: This is a CCP.\par \par \