is in amplifying the anti-White agenda of the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 In his e-mail, which is virtually illiterate, Suarez announces that DEI is now the guiding idea at \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  . The word "safety" never makes an appearance.\par \par \uc2 This is a huge change in the way that airlines operate and Suarez seems to understand that some people who work at Southwest will be nervous about it.\par \par \uc2 But Juan Suarez has a solution. Southwest pilots are not allowed to, "resent or question" the skills of colleagues who have been promoted on the basis of strict race and gender based affirmative action quotas. Henceforth, pilots must ignore incompetence. That's going to solve the problem.\par \par \uc2 But will it solve the problem? Not allowing people to notice that their copilots are incompetent? Well, as one veteran Southwest pilot put it: "A core tenant of commercial aviation is to avoid distractions and prioritize tasks that foster a safe flight. Now, the company is purposefully distracting pilots with something completely unrelated to the safety of flight. This is criminal negligence. Spending millions of dollars on this when we're having runway incursions and near misses is insane."\par \par \uc2 Yes, it is insane. And as we've said before, with both sadness and certainty, at some point, many people are going to die because of this. Unfortunately, that's true.\par \par \uc2 So the drama in the banking sector, the collapse of \uc2 Silicon Valley Bank\uc2  has a lot of Americans concerned about how to protect their money and of course, politicians are using that concern to their advantage, as always.\par \par \uc2 Several States are now trying to centralize currency with a so-called Central Bank Digital Currency, which is, by the way, not currency at all. It's software. But they're going to do it for your own good. Obviously, this is a tool of total social control.\par \par \uc2 If they control your money, if they can zero out your bank account with a keystroke, then you have no autonomy. They control you.\par \par \uc2 Well, in the State of South Dakota, legislators just passed a bill that would have changed the definition of money to exclude cryptocurrency, and that would put the state on a path to Centralized Digital Currency.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota's Governor, Kristi, Noem, the only Governor we're aware of who is paying attention to this vetoed that bill. She joins us tonight to explain why.\par \par \uc2 Governor, thank you very much for doing this first, and for coming on. Why did you do it? You're obviously under pressure not to veto it, but you did. Why did you?\par \par \uc2 GOV. KRISTI NOEM (R-SD): While Tucker, it was the right thing to do. I became aware of this bill. It wasn't introduced until almost halfway through our legislative session.\par \par \uc2 We started reading through this bill that was over 110 pages long. It was sold as an update to the guidelines of the Universal Commercial Code backed by all of our financial institutions, our banks.\par \par \uc2 As we started reading through it, we saw the section of the bill that changed the definition of currency, and essentially what it did was paved the way for a government-led CBDC and it also banned any other form of cryptocurrency or Bitcoin or digital currency that existed. So for me, it very clearly was a threat to our freedom.\par \par \uc2 In South Dakota, we are the session that completes its business earliest in the year. We are the first ones to really look at this bill and find out the truth of what's in it, and I did veto that bill.\par \par \uc2 I'm asking my legislators to change their minds, to make the right decision and help me kill this bill once and for all. But I'm telling you, Tucker, we've got the same language coming to over 20 other States. I believe it's to pave a way for the Federal government to control our currency and thus control people.\par \par \uc2 It should be alarming to everyone and it's being sold as a UCC Guidelines Update.\par \par \uc2 There is no rush to do this. We need to be smart and make sure that we're doing what we can to protect people.\par \par \uc2 I find it ironic that we also are having this discussion at the same time we have banks and credit card companies talking about coding gun and ammunition in a separate code so they can track it.\par \par \uc2 So not only can they tie these two issues together, if the government doesn't approve of what you're purchasing, if they have the only form of digital currency out there that is endorsed and utilized in the country, they can control how you spend that money and thus, take away all your freedom.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It is so nicely put, and I don't think you're overstating at all the significance of this.\par \par \uc2 Really quickly, do you think and you want to give everyone the benefit of the doubt on their motives -- but do you think that legislators in your State understand what this bill was actually designed to do?\par \par \uc2 NOEM: You don't know if they read it, Tucker, that is what is alarming to me. It was over 110 pages long and they were told by lobbyists that they had listened to for the last 20 years that it's fine. It's just a regulation update. This is what we do is adopt Federal regulations.\par \par \uc2 But if you start reading it, you see in there, there is a redefinition of currency that it says government, CBDCs are okay if they're run by the government, but any other form is then banned.\par \par \uc2 It is clearly a change for how people's assets are utilized. It clearly limits the freedom of people to use other forms of currency that they may choose to if it is a digital currency and it is clearly putting power into the hands of government.\par \par \uc2 If anything, we should have learned the last several years is the government can't be trusted. You know, Tucker, what I was surprised by was that you know, the bills that have made it to my desk this year, 