 hey, thank you for trying. You're out. We've got to narrow this field and go forward. So we try to give folk as lot of confidence that this is not going to be a repeat of 16 where a diluted field has one candidate winning at 25 percent.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Is that rose-colored glasses by the Governor of New Hampshire?\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: From his lips to the candidates' ears. Is he willing to say if you're not polling, I'm out? That's the big question.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: That was intonation.\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: It seemed to be. Look, he is absolutely right. And look, I think everybody who wants to try it out should go in. It's a free country. If you want to run for president, go ahead and throw your hat in the ring and see if you can gather some enthusiasm. But the problem is in 2016 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the nomination with a third the electorate, right. And you even saw that playing out in some of the primaries where he endorsed candidates who won with 32 percent when 68 percent of the state was against his chosen candidates.\par \par \uc2 So if these people get in the race -- he didn't get above 50 percent until the New York primary in answer April 19th. So he won the nomination with a third the vote. He could do that again if we don't have the discipline. So, candidates should go in, test the waters. And if you don't catch a wave, get out of the race.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So the former president, very active this weekend on Truth Social, called this network the RINO network. He also said about Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , "Florida was doing great long before Ron DeSanctus got there." "DeSanctimonious" is the word he uses. "People are fleeing from New York to Florida and other places because of high taxes and out of control crime, not because of Governor (thank you President Trump!) DeSanctimonious. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  did great. Even \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  had very good numbers. Sunshine and ocean, very alluring." \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , of course, the Democrat that he ran against, DeSantis did, and defeated soundly.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: President Trump never shies away from nicknaming his opponents. DeSantis has not declared even though it's clear he may be getting in given his countrywide crime tour. Interesting how he has treated Nikki Haley, not a whole lot of nicknames on that.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Yet.\par \par \uc2 PAVLICH: But he has 40 percent -- yet. But he has 40 percent of the voters in the Republican Party as of now. And if there are a number of candidates who stay in for far too long and their goal as candidates is to beat him, the math doesn't add up.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: But quickly, Josh, the Republican Party probably has a little angst with these see these posts.\par \par \uc2 KRAUSHAAR: They do. But going back to Sununu, likability matters. Haley had a very optimistic message, she is likeable. Sununu put on a good face here on the show tonight. Trump and DeSantis, that's their biggest vulnerability.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, thank you all.\par \par \uc2 It's Tuesday. It's time for "Tuesday Tweets." First up, Dan asks, "Bret, does Biden visit to Ukraine put pressure on GOP presidential candidates to take a stand on support for Ukraine?" One-hundred percent. It's a question out there, if the president is out visiting and talking like he is talking, it will be a major issue as you head into this race.\par \par \uc2 Next up, Dr. Strangelove tweets, "Do you think the Biden administration will include F-16 fighter jets in a future Ukrainian aid package?" Hard to see right now. They have said no. But we have seen this evolution of all of this stuff.\par \par \uc2 Last, Cindy wants to know, "Who is your favorite "FIVE" host that transitions from their show to yours?" It's kind of like a box of chocolates. You never know what's going to be in there. Greg usually has the biggest surprises on the handover.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and still unafraid. "JESSE WATTERS PRIMETIME" starts right now. Jesse is pretty good on the handover.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020230222ej2l00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Americans Deserve A Say On The War In Ukraine; Biden Too Busy In Ukraine To Visit East Palestine; GOP Silent While Biden Ignores East Palestine; People In East Palestine Are Scared And Afraid; Roald Dahl's Classic Children's Book Censored; Don Lemon Still Missing From His Show; Florida Residents Facing Fallout From Major Fires; Bill Introduced In The House To Publicly Disclose All JFK Records; Interview With Rep. \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2  (R-AZ); Layoffs And Hiring Freezes In Corporate America; New AI Robot Is Already Hinting At Nuking The Planet And Starting A Pandemic\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Tulsi Gabbard, Trace Gallagher, Charlie Gasparino \par \uc2 7,845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 February 2023\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Love your bumper music. Big thumbs up for the Tower of Power keeping the funk alive.\par \par \uc2 think I'm the only show in cable that plays funk, and we want to keep it that way for us.\par \par \uc2 DVR us. Tucker is up next.\par \par \uc2 And always remember, I'm Watters. This is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT. Happy Monday.\par \par \uc2 People used to tell you that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was stupid. Remember that? "He's an idiot." Now, we're not going to sit here and tell you it was a smart idea to turn the White House over to \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 ; it was not. But it's also true if we're being honest -- and we should be -- that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had far wiser instincts about American foreign policy than any leader in at least a generation, and he did it without the help of anyone.\par \par \uc2 None of his advisers wanted to hear his views on foreign policy. In fact, they desperately wanted Trump to be quiet, but Trump wouldn't. "What's the point of \uc2 NATO\uc2 ?" He asked, nearly 30 years after the fall of the Soviet Union. No one in Washington could answer him. "Shut up, racist," they replied.\par \par \uc2 But Trump just kept going in his Trumpy way. "Why would we fight Russia?" He wondered. "Wouldn't making Russia our enemy just drive Putin into the arms of China and create the most powerful and dangerous anti-American bloc in history?"\par \par \uc2 No one bothered to answer him. In fact, for the sin of asking, they called him a traitor to his country. They impeached him for it, and then they started a war with Putin.\par \par \uc2 But in retrospect, Trump had asked a deeply patriotic question: If Russia ever joined forces with China, American global hegemony, its power would end instantly. You'd have the world's largest land mass and largest natural gas reserves, allied with the world's largest population and world's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 So, a Russia-China axis would be not just more powerful than the United States, but much more powerful. It would have the scale to control a lot of the world's economy and trade routes and raw materials. It could project military force that posturing aside, we actually don't have the power to stop.\par \par \uc2 If Russia and China ever got together, it would be a brand-new world and the United States would be greatly diminished. Most Americans agree that would be bad.\par \par \uc2 Now, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  predicted very clearly, that is happening. Thanks to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's reckless and self-destructive response to the invasion of Ukraine a year ago this week, the economies of Russia and China are intertwined.\par \par \uc2 Chinese spending on Russian goods has increased by more than 60 percent. China now imports more coal from Russia than it has in the last five years. Chinese shipments to Russia, meanwhile, are up by nearly 30 percent.\par \par \uc2 Companies like \uc2 Ford\uc2  and \uc2 Toyota\uc2  pulled out of Russia. They had to. Remember that? So, what happened next? Chinese automakers stepped in.\par \par \uc2 Chinese carmakers once made less than 10 percent of all cars bought in Russia. Now, China makes a third of them, and you can see where this is going. The same thing has happened with smartphones and countless other consumer goods.\par \par \uc2 Not surprisingly, the Chinese yuan is replacing the dollar in Moscow. Chinese currency now accounts for fully one-fifth of all trades on the Moscow Stock Exchange. That's up from less than one percent last year.\par \par \uc2 So, these are deep and growing economic ties and they're formal. The thing about economic ties, however, is that they lead inexorably to military ties. So, it shouldn't surprise you that China is actively helping Russia in the war against \uc2 NATO\uc2 , which we are leading.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the country with more ships than any navy in the world has united with a country that has more nuclear armed ICBMs than any country in the world to fight us through proxy in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Well, that's scary, and the thing is, everybody involved seems to know it's scary and just how scary it is. Our leaders understand that their push for total war with Putin, which is unnecessary, could lead to the destruction of the West. They know that, but they're doing it anyway.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with a German newspaper today, the Ukrainian President Zelenskyy casually mentioned that, oh, by the way, the entire world may soon go up in flames: "If China aligns itself with Russia, there will be a World War."\par \par \uc2 There will be a world war if China aligns with Russia? Who could say something like that calmly, since as we just told you, China is aligned with Russia? It's already happened. That's not speculation. It's a fact. And as a result of that fact, according to Zelenskyy himself, hundreds of millions of people will die. No big deal, as long as we take Crimea. This is a very dark way of thinking.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy himself is a very dark force. That is obvious if you watch him. It is unmistakable. Who could not see that? This man is a destroyer. He banned a Christian faith in his country and arrested nuns and priests.\par \par \uc2 Oh, but he's a hero, claim our leaders from \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  to \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 . No, Zelenskyy is not a hero. He is an instrument of total destruction. That is not a defense of his enemies. It's just true and maybe that's why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is drawn to him. Biden landed in Kyiv today to promote another World War. Watch.\par \par \uc2 [VIDEO CLIP PLAYS]\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Note the air-raid sirens in the background. What's strange is there didn't seem to be any air raids in Kyiv this morning. We checked. There were just air-raid sirens at precisely the moment that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appeared for a photo-op. Even CNN's reporters on the ground in Kyiv know that they've been in the city for the past five days and didn't hear any bombs or missile strikes or any sirens until the moment that Biden walked out for the cameras.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEX MARQUARDT, CNN SENIOR NATIONAL SECURITY CORRESPONDENT: I've been here for the past five days. I have not heard any explosions. I have not heard any air sirens until about half an hour ago, right when President Biden was in the center of Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Right. So, here you have Potemkin air-raid sirens, just the touch required in this, the most tightly scripted, most completely dishonest war in history, the fakest war and the point, of course, is to sell Americans on yet another $500 million in tax dollars for Ukraine, for the Zelenskyy government. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We've committed nearly 700 tanks and thousands of armored vehicles, 1,000 artillery systems, more than two million rounds of artillery ammunition, more than 50 advanced launch rocket systems, anti-ship and air defense systems, all defending -- to defend Ukraine and that doesn't count the other half a billion dollars we're going to be -- we're announcing with you today and tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 That's going to be coming your way and that's just the United States in this piece.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Can anyone see how dark and crazy this is, truly crazy? Yes, many Americans can see how dark and crazy it is. Look at the numbers.\par \par \uc2 How many Americans support this war for democracy? This war for democracy that Americans for some reason can't vote on? Why don't we have a national referendum on all this? As long as we're leveling a country on behalf of democracy, it might be nice to try democracy here, but no. It's all so grotesque. It defies imagination, really.\par \par \uc2 But imagine if you were watching all of this, the spectacle from your home in East Palestine, Ohio, a home that is still stinking of chemicals you can't identify.\par \par \uc2 So here you have the President of the United States, personally visiting a corrupt foreign autocrat to announce a half a billion dollars more in your tax dollars to go to Ukraine. Meanwhile, you, stuck in some lost and forgotten part of Ohio, the State that helped build this country, have a mushroom cloud over your city. The animals are dying. The water is glowing.\par \par \uc2 And yet, for more than two weeks after all of this started with the famous train derailment, FEMA and the Biden administration have refused to provide any kind of financial assistance to you.\par \par \uc2 East Palestine still hasn't even gotten a visit, a token visit, from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's token Transportation Secretary, Mayor Pete, and after two weeks, people in East Palestine are starting to notice. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: What Federal response?\par \par \uc2 FOX NEWS CHANNEL REPORTER: The White House is under fire for its response to the East Palestine train derailment.\par \par \uc2 EAST PALESTINE RESIDENT: If it were in Washington, DC, it would all be cleaned up and taken care of.\par \par \uc2 EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: I've had massive headaches since it started\par \par \uc2 ABC NEWS REPORTER: And locals say they're feeling the effects of the toxic chemicals.\par \par \uc2 ROXANA SABERI, \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS CORRESPONDENT: East Palestine resident, Melissa Blake says two days after that toxic train derailment, doctors diagnosed her with acute bronchitis from chemical fumes.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA BLAKE, EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: It's hard to breathe. My chest is always tight, the coughing.\par \par \uc2 JOE MORRIS, EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: I'm 53. I've had two headaches in my life, and I feel like I've had one every day since the controlled burn.\par \par \uc2 SHELBY WALKER, EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: My kids will never go play in our backyard again, which makes me very sad. Now, it is never going to be safe for them in my eyes.\par \par \uc2 SABERI: Today, families like the Bailes lined up for a $1,000.00 check per person.\par \par \uc2 Is $1,000.00 enough?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL BAILES, EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: Probably not. Honestly, it is probably not.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL GEORGE, \uc2 CBS\uc2  NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Ted Murphy doesn't believe officials who say there's no lingering health risks.\par \par \uc2 TED MURPHY, EAST PALESTINE, OHIO RESIDENT: I've got to move because I'm not safe being here. There is no way we are safe.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: But nobody cares and they know that in East Palestine. But the contrasts are becoming too sharp and obvious: The American border versus the Ukrainian border. One doesn't matter at all. In fact, it's racist. The other is so important we'll risk nuclear war to protect it.\par \par \uc2 Aid to Zelenskyy? Unaudited. God knows where it's going. Nobody seems to care. And Aid to East Palestine, we just can't afford it.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the people, you just saw are not Ukrainian, so \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not interested enough to visit. Unfortunately, no one in East Palestine thought to pay \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's son 80 grand a month. If someone had done that, if someone had been wise enough to pay off the Biden family eight years ago, things would be different. Here's how \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  might talk to them now.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: It's going to deliver much needed humanitarian assistance as well as food, water, medicine, shelter and other aid to Ukrainians displaced by Russia's war and provide aid for those seeking refuge in other countries from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 It is also going to help schools and hospitals open. It's going to allow pensions and social support to be paid to the Ukrainian people so they have something, something, in their pocket.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, not everything that winds its way through Congress is of equal importance. Most legislation in Congress means nothing in the long term. Nuclear war means everything in the long term.\par \par \uc2 So, what's the issue on which both parties seem aligned? Oh, the issue that matters.\par \par \uc2 So, there is no opposition party. Both parties seem to agree that the administration that shot down weather balloons with $400,000.00 heat- seeking missiles is capable of navigating an incredibly complex conflict in Eastern Europe, where the stakes are existential. No problem. We can pull this off. Everybody involved is Winston Churchill.\par \par \uc2 No one on the Republican side seems outraged on a gut level that the President of the United States is personally visiting an autocrat in a tracksuit in Kyiv while he ignores the exposure of thousands of American citizens to toxic chemicals we can't identify.\par \par \uc2 So, Republicans in the Senate have a leader. You might be interested in what he thinks is important. Here he is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. MITCH MCCONNELL (R-KY): I'm going to try to help explain to the American people that defeating the Russians in Ukraine is the single most important event going on in the world right now.\par \par \uc2 It will save us an enormous amount of money down the road if the Ukrainians can succeed. They are not asking for any of our personnel. They're asking us for financial help.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, the thing is, that's not rhetoric. \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  believes what he just said. "I'm going to help explain." You couldn't help explain how to get from here to the nearest gas station. You're beyond the ability to explain, and you're way beyond the ability to lead the opposition in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 .\par \pa