LL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020230215ej2e00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 House Panel Stresses Growing China Threat; Lawmakers To Receive China Spy Flight Briefings; More Children Rescued After Deadly Earthquakes; Rep. Kevin McCarthy (R-CA) Is Being Interviewed About The Extent Of Chinese Spy Activities; Enes Freedom On Devastating Earthquake In Turkey; China's Human Rights Abuses Left Out Of Biden SOTU; Enes Freedom: Biden Has Been Soft On Dictators; DOD: China Spy Flights Over At Least Five Continents; McCarthy: Failing To Speak As One Voice On China; Speaker McCarthy: China Spying Is Not New; Kevin McCarthy On Biden's State Of The Union; Biden Touts Economy In Visit To Battleground WI; Biden Blasted For "Misleading" Econ Claims In SOTU; Biden Pushes More Spending As Prices Remain High; Zelenskyy Asks For Fighter Jets During UK Visit\b0\par\par\uc2 Martha MacCallum, Aishah Hasnie, Greg Palkot. Kellyanne Conway;  Juan Williams; Trey Yingst \par \uc2 8,936 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 February 2023\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: The Story with Martha MacCallum\par \uc2 HUNDD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2023 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2023 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JOHN ROBERTS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST (on camera): Yes. OK, well, let's see what it's like tomorrow. When you're on a bed, it's completely different than it is today.\par \par \uc2 SANDRA SMITH, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: All right.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: I mean, every day, it's like, it's down then it's up. I'm pessimistic today and I'm optimistic tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: Well, we will head into the latter half of the week now, finishing this Wednesday. Thanks for joining us. I'm Sandra Smith.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: And I'm John Roberts. We'll see you again tomorrow. THE STORY with Martha starts right now.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Thank you very much, you, guys. Good afternoon, everybody. I'm Martha MacCallum live in our nation's capital. The Speaker of the House, Kevin McCarthy, joins us live this hour with his reaction to the State of the Union address last night which he witnessed at very close proximity, why he says the president is goading Republicans with that State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 Plus, also we'll talk about what he just learned about the China spy flight in a classified hearing, a classified testimony that took place earlier today. Very hot topic for the House panel that is probing the most pressing threats that face the U.S. today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GEN. PETER PERTRAEUS, FORMER CIA DIRECTOR: We should recognize that Beijing seeks to divide the Euro-Atlantic Alliance.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: That is a serious question, if Beijing is seeking to divide us from our allies. We're going to talk about that. In moments, House Republicans also today, busy day, on the hill as things get, get rolling the beginning of this February. They are grilling former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  executives. This is quite a lineup they've got on the company's "role in suppressing the Hunter Biden laptop story" and how they came to those conclusions.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM JORDAN (R-OH): I think you guys got played by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Five days after, you guys take down the Hunter Biden story. 51 former intel officials send a letter and they say the Hunter Biden story has all the classic earmarks of a Russian information operation. The information operation was run on you guys.\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): We could be talking about abortion rights, civil rights, voting rights, but instead, we're talking about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's have fake laptop story.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Very testy hearings going on, on the hill today. Congressman \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2  is the chair of the House Intel Committee. So, a lot on his plate today. He's also on the Oversight Committee where you saw those clips from with Jim Jordan, he is going to join us in just moments. But first a Congressional Correspondent Aishah Hasnie, covering this live on Capitol Hill. Hi, Aishah.\par \par \uc2 AISHAH HASNIE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Hey there, Martha. Good afternoon to you. I can tell you that Fox can now confirm that tomorrow, every single lawmaker in the House and the Senate will receive a classified briefing, intelligence briefing on this Chinese spy flight. In fact, this morning, some House leaders already got their closed-door briefing, which shows really, the urgency of the matter, even though last night during the State of the Union speech, the President did not mention the CCP until about an hour into the speech, Martha, and when he did, it was just about 200 words of the 7000-plus words that he spoke. Democrats defended the President, while Republicans say, he really missed the moment here to galvanize the bipartisanship on the hill when it comes to China.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA): I think that was a missed opportunity for certain we've got to push back on the bully. China is almost a peer-to-peer adversary when you project weakness invites aggression, and that's what we're inviting from China.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (voiceover): Now, lawmakers on both sides of the aisle are trying to learn more as the Pentagon tells us today the balloon was part of a larger Chinese surveillance program that is based in China's high nine province. Tomorrow, Democrat Senator \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  will move forward with holding a defense appropriation hearing to get to the bottom of what happened here at home.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HASNIE (on camera): So, much more to come on all of this. Martha.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Thank you very much, Aishah. Aishah Hasnie on Capitol Hill. Congressman \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 , as I said, Chairman of the House Intelligence Committee, he also sits on the Oversight Committee that is handling the business at \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and why they were sitting on the Hunter Biden story right before the election. Congressman, Chairman, great to have you with us. Thank you for being here today. So, so you sat in on this hearing, oversaw this intel hearing. And you had a panel in front of you, including General Petraeus talking about the greatest threats that face the nation. And we just heard from Aishah's report, the President spent 200 words, talking about China last night. Was that appropriate given what you heard today?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 MIKE TURNER\uc2  (R-OH): Absolutely not, the whole world was captivated by this balloon that was going over some of our most sensitive military sites in our country, doing surveillance spying, and you know, we don't know exactly what else the, the balloon and its equipment was doing. This administration was slow to intervene. They waited until after he completed his whole mission. So, all of its collection had occurred before they took any action after it gotten off at the Atlantic Coast.\par \par \uc2 Our panel today, were experts: Heather Wilson, General Breedlove, Sue Gordon, and of course, General Petraeus. To give us some perspective of what do we need to be looking for with the intelligence community on the issue of China, and what we heard from them was a broad range of threats what they're doing in their nuclear weapons expansion what they're doing in space and of course, what they're doing in violating our own airspace and sovereignty with this spy balloon.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. So, what did they recommend? And did they approve of the action that the President took this week?\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Well, you know, our, our area of inquiry was on the intelligence gathering. And so, we didn't really press them on, should he have done it before, after except they, they did on their own offer, that they should have never been allowed to go over the United States. So that, so, clearly, you know, they had the same angst that we did, which is why was this balloon allowed to complete its mission? Why did the President make that decision? On China, they think, on full scale, both economic and intelligence and militarily that we need to push back that China is preparing itself as an aggressor nation, to threaten the United States and our allies. And then if we don't push back, we don't meet this threat, that there could be tragic consequence.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And did you feel on, on the committee, you know, we heard from another member of Congress moments ago, who said that this is clearly a bipartisan mission in terms of understanding the threat from China. Do you get that sense on this committee that both sides are aligned on how to approach this?\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Absolutely. And one of the things that as Chairman that I've dedicated myself to is returning the Intelligence Committee back to a bipartisan focus and to focus on national security, taking it from the Adam Schiff legacy of when he was handling impeachment inappropriately. With that, we have bipartisan support for that. Yesterday, when we began our committee's work, both the minority leader and the speaker came and gave us the charge that both from a Democratic or Republican leadership perspective, they want this committee to do its work and its work as national security.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: OK, so Jim Comer on the other committee that you're on, was grilling, really the top brass at \uc2 Twitter\uc2  who made all the decisions? And I have to say, many of these moments were very embarrassing for them. At one point, Nancy Mace asked one of them, what's your medical degree? Where did you get it from, asking questions about why you would remove other doctors' assessments of COVID from \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ? This one had to do with what kind of legal advice they sought when they decided to pull down the Hunter Biden story. This is an exchange with James Comer, the Chairman of the Committee, and \uc2 Vijaya Gadde\uc2 , the Chief, former Chief Legal Officer at \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , she was fired by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 COMER: Ms. Gadde, when the New York Post initially broke the story about the laptop, did you call \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's lawyer to ask if it was authentic?\par \par \uc2 VIJAYA GADDE\uc2 , FORMER CHIEF LEGAL OFFICER AT TWITTER: No, I did not.\par \par \uc2 COMER\uc2 : You're telling this committee that, that you didn't ask any Biden representative if the laptop was real, or for \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's attorneys phone number to confirm its authenticity.\par \par \uc2 GADDE: We did not speak to anybody related to that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes, because they'd already spoken to people who told them, if you ever see anything like this, you have to pull it down immediately, did absolutely zero according to her due diligence of their own.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: There was a lot of wrongdoing, obviously, at \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . But the thing that's very concerning, which is what we have to get to the bottom within this, in these hearings, is what was your government doing? You know, our committee, Intelligence Committee was organized for the purposes to protect Americans from their intelligence Committee doing nefarious acts. And now we're seeing them, and we're getting the testimony from industry of how they've been approached by government to take actions and actions that are inappropriate.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Thank you very much, Chairman \uc2 Mike Turner\uc2 . Always good to have you with us. Nice to have you in the studio today. Thanks for coming over from all the way over there. Good to see you. All right. So, as I mentioned, Speaker Kevin McCarthy will join us exclusively. We're also going to talk to his guest at the State of the Union, Human Rights Activist and Professional Basketball Player, Enes Kanter Freedom after his slam dunk on LeBron James, "bow down to China" next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Just incredible video of these little kids being pulled out from under the rubble and people cheering after these devastating earthquakes in Syria and Turkey. The crew in this video spent more than a day searching for the family that they finally found trapped under the rubble in Syria. The quakes have now killed more than 11,000 people. This little girl coming out after the little girl that we saw just incredibly moving photos and video that we're seeing. So, that number of course could keep rising as the search for victims goes on and hopefully more survivors to come.\par \par \uc2 Former NBA Player, Enes Kanter Freedom, is from Turkey, and he will join us in just a moment. First, to Senior Foreign Affairs Correspondent Greg Palkot reporting live from Gaziantep, Turkey. Hi, Greg.\par \par \uc2 GREG PALKOT, FOX NEWS CHANNEL SENIOR FOREIGN AFFAIRS CORRESPONDENT: Hey, Martha. Yes, it has been a long day and night here in Gaziantep. A struggle playing out here as it is playing out throughout the region. I'm going to step aside and let my cameraman, Ben, show you the scene. When we 