that definitely with them.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: And you were guest of the Speaker. We have a picture of the two of you together last night in his office before the address. And I wonder, you know, if you were surprised that the president didn't mention the earthquake, he has mentioned it today, I should point out.\par \par \uc2 FREEDOM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Here some images of you guys, before you went into that room and watched?\par \par \uc2 FREEDOM: Well, I mean, he knew I was there. And, he knew I was there. I guess, second most important guest in that State of the Union after first lady.\par \par \uc2 But, you know, I just wish that he's had something. Because I'm sure that so many people wanted to hear what the most powerful men in the world had to say.\par \par \uc2 But, you know, that is definitely heartbreaking. I just definitely wish that he said something.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: You obviously have spoken out against China and the \uc2 NBA\uc2 's cozy economic relationship that they continue to perpetuate with China.\par \par \uc2 Nothing on the Uighurs last night, nothing on human trafficking. None of those subjects came up. Why do you think that is?\par \par \uc2 FREEDOM: Well, I mean, it's not a lie that I think President Biden has been soft against some of the dictatorships out there. Like Turkey, like China. And I was actually just waited to hear the words of human rights. You know, because there's so many people out there, especially the people in China, like Uyghurs that are right now, there are two 3 million Uighur people are in concentration camp in China, getting torture and raped every day.\par \par \uc2 So, I was here, I was waiting to hear the word of human rights that are coming out of his mouth, but unfortunately, did not.\par \par \uc2 Is that a lie that he's been soft, but we definitely have to hold them accountable.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Erdogan is in a difficult position right now. He wants to maintain his power in the 