 our country.\par \par \uc2 FREEDOM: Thank you so much. I'll (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, thank you. It's great to have you here.\par \par \uc2 FREEDOM: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM (voice over): So, coming up, China's spy aircraft may have been used to collect information on massive amounts of U.S. military capabilities.\par \par \uc2 We are learning a lot about this story. And there was a behind closed doors briefing today that Kevin McCarthy took place in. Speaker of the House, he is -- has just arrived here, and he will tell us -- give us a sense of what we're learning now about the extent of Chinese spy activities. It's not just one balloon folks.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM (on camera): What is China really up to so a classified briefing today on Capitol Hill and more to come on the Chinese spy flight that was shot down on Saturday, just outside of the U.S. borders. Now, the spy craft -- or within the ocean border, I should say.\par \par \uc2 Part of the "vast" surveillance program that has been run by the People's Liberation Army that has "operated" for several years, over five continents around the globe.\par \par \uc2 But somehow, we didn't hear anything about the extent of this program last night from the president, or what the people should be aware of in this country. He made only a scant handful of mentions even if China and the growing threat that they pose to all of us here in the United States.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I'm committed to work with China where we can advance American interests and benefit the world. But make no mistake about it, as we made clear last week, if China threatens our sovereignty, we will act to protect our country, and we did.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, sort of a new tableau there last night, House -- Speaker of the House Kevin McCarthy, right behind the president on the podium there. And he was in that behind closed doors briefing on the China threat.\par \par \uc2 Speaker McCarthy, very good to have you here this morning. Thank you -- this afternoon, I should say.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 REP. KEVIN MCCARTHY (R-CA): Thanks for letting me back up.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Thanks for being here. So, this is \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reporting, and our Pentagon reporters have confirmed this, that this program is actually massive, this Chinese intelligence program.\par \par \uc2 These balloons are part of a vast aerial surveillance program, been around for several years. I think we have pictures of the balloons that have been flying over this country over the past six years. And it goes over five continents outfitted with electro optical -- electro optical sensors, digital cameras, capturing highly precise images, satellite transmission capability, the whole nine yards.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: Well, it should make us even more concerned. I mean, think about this, China actually acknowledged, yes, is, their balloon. And then, they had the boldness to say after it was shut down, after it's gone over our sovereignty that they want it back.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it's very important that we do capture it, find out what's on it, find out what they are doing. But they did put out publicly the American Intel to the public that this isn't the only one that it's also in other continents as well.\par \par \uc2 This is what China has been doing. But it should be no doubt to us. This is a reason why I -- when we became Speaker, I selected and created a new committee on China, put an equal number of Republicans and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 What I think we have really failed as a country is when we don't speak with one voice to China. We've become dependent in so many areas. Be at critical minerals, they are looking at our -- stealing our farmland, you look at our intel -- intellectual property that they continue to take.\par \par \uc2 This has got to stop, but they are so bold to go over our country, even though we know that it's coming and we tell the public, shoot it down, and they want it back.\par \par \uc2 Think about it. How far they've gone? They developed a relationship with a person who became a member of Congress on the Intel Committee, but they created that relationship all the way back when he was a city councilman when \uc2 Eric Swalwell\uc2  were there.\par \par \uc2 That takes a lot of money, a lot of resources. Feinstein, the senator of California, her driver for a decade was a Chinese spy.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: So, why do we think this is new? This is something they have planned for a long time. And then, we just see President Xi changed the Constitution, keep himself in power, and then, just tell his country to be prepare to invade Taiwan by 2027.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: But can't that the president barely mentions it last night.\par \par \uc2 And I think, people listened to all this. They put all those things together that you're putting together. And they say, why isn't this a huge focus of the State of the Union address?\par \par \uc2 Here is another thing that is catching a lot of attention. What about these UFOs or UFPs, as they're called, that the Pentagon has been telling us, we're not exactly sure what these are.\par \par \uc2 Holman Jenkins, writing in The Wall Street Journal today, "national security agencies were using UFOs to hide something they didn't want us to see. That something, it has slowly dribbled out since May, was Chinese surveillance in U.S. airspace.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: But it's not just there. They're on our campuses. They actually try to go in and influence American citizens who are dissident. You just had a guest on your show that they tried to silence and not let him play basketball anymore because he stands up for freedom.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Right.\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: This is something that countries should wake up. And this is where the president failed. Because in every single kitchen table, I will promise you last week, they were talking about this Chinese spy balloon. They were taking pictures of it seeing itself.\par \par \uc2 It's not something so far up in space, you cannot see. I had an own congressman watching it when it was shut down from his porch.\par \par \uc2 This is the atrocity that's happening here to America. And if we don't speak stronger, China will continue to do that.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: But, would you argue for decoupling? I mean, we heard the president, the beginning of those comments last night, he said, well, we want to work together in places where we can.\par \par \uc2 I mean, I had to wonder, when I look at this, really, I mean, we still have to work together in places where we have common interests. Do we have common interests at this point?\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: I think they have been proven that China does not have common interest with us. They don't have the same belief and freedom.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, why are we still saying it? Why is the president saying that?\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY: That's a big question, because he is harming our nation. It's kind of like what Secretary of Defense Gates' said. Almost every decision that Biden has made in his elected office, foreign policy has been wrong. And we've watched it time and again, and I think he's failing here. Because why does China feel that they could come over our sovereign nation in our airspace?\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Because they can. They've been doing it for years, apparently.\par \par \uc2 From the very first mile it would come in, it should have been shut down.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: So, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  was asked what she thought about last night. Must have been very different for her to watch you up there with the gavel. You didn't rip up any speeches, I noticed.\par \par 