e are getting very rich from this. That's why Washington supports it. And very soon, we're going to give you a case study on who exactly is getting rich from it, some of the people who are promoting this war that is killing an endless number of Ukrainians are personally benefiting from it and you should know that.\par \par \uc2 But the cost to us is profound. In fact, we're sending so much military equipment to Ukraine, to Zelenskyy and his wife, that we are running out of weapons for our own military to defend our own country. And that's not a guess.\par \par \uc2 The Secretary of the Navy, \uc2 Carlos Del Toro\uc2  just said that out loud: "With regards to deliveries of weapons systems for the fight in Ukraine. Yes, that's always a concern for us. If the conflict does go on for six months or another year, it certainly continues to stress the supply chain in ways that are challenging." In other words, you can either defend Ukraine's borders or you can defend the United States of America. Which is it?\par \par \uc2 Well, most Members of Congress are choosing Ukraine, which tells you everything, but a small number coming to their senses. In the House, \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  of Kentucky is one of them.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. THOMAS MASSIE (R-KY): We've spent more in Ukraine, the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  has, than we spend on all of our roads and bridges in an entire year, the entire infrastructure of this country, the roads and bridges, the real infrastructure, we don't spend as much on that here as we've spent on Ukraine in nine months.\par \par \uc2 I think that's despicable. Our priorities are all out of whack.\par \par \uc2 And I'll finish with this: We're trying to get the documents here to find out where that money went. What we really need is a full audit.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So this is a crime against our country being perpetrated by the Democratic Party with the full buy-in of most Republicans, but 